{"jobs":[{"id":"22fe890a-5c2c-4133-a91c-2e82348bc5d8","title":"Software Engineer II, Cloud Platform","department":"All Departments","team":"Cloud Platform Team","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"US California (Redwood City) - Office","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-18T23:22:32.317+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Redwood City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/22fe890a-5c2c-4133-a91c-2e82348bc5d8","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/22fe890a-5c2c-4133-a91c-2e82348bc5d8/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Poshmark</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Poshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection.</strong> Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2>🎯 About the Role</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a Software Engineer II to join our Core Platform team and contribute to</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">building reliable, high-performance backend systems that power our fast-growing</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">marketplace. This is an exciting opportunity to work with experienced engineers and gain</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">hands-on experience developing cloud-native services used by millions of users every day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>⚙️ What You’ll Do</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, develop, and maintain backend services that support Poshmark’s marketplace experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with peers and senior engineers to implement scalable, efficient, and maintainable systems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write clean, well-documented, and well-tested code following best practices.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in code reviews and learn from feedback to continually improve.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot and fix issues across distributed systems in production environments.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to improving development processes, tooling, and team workflows.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>6-Month Accomplishments:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Become proficient with Poshmark’s tech stack, development tools, and codebase.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ship production-quality code with guidance from senior team members.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Take ownership of small to medium-sized components or features.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate effectively with Product, QA, and Design teams on feature delivery.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>12+ Month Accomplishments:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Independently deliver features from design to production.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to performance improvements and scalability initiatives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop a strong understanding of Poshmark’s system architecture and make data-driven technical decisions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in technical discussions and contribute ideas to improve platform reliability and efficiency.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor interns or new hires joining the team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>💪 What You’ll Bring</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2 - 4 years of professional experience (including internships) in backend software engineering.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of computer science fundamentals — data structures, algorithms, and software design principles.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficiency in at least one backend language (e.g., Ruby, Java, Python, or Go).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with RESTful APIs, databases (SQL/NoSQL), and caching or message-queue systems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interest in cloud technologies (AWS, GCP, or similar) and scalable architectures.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborative, curious, and motivated to learn and grow within a fast-paced environment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT POSHMARK\n\n\nPoshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection. Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.\n\n \n\n\n🎯 ABOUT THE ROLE\n\nWe are looking for a Software Engineer II to join our Core Platform team and contribute to\n\nbuilding reliable, high-performance backend systems that power our fast-growing\n\nmarketplace. This is an exciting opportunity to work with experienced engineers and gain\n\nhands-on experience developing cloud-native services used by millions of users every day.\n\n\n\n\n⚙️ WHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nDesign, develop, and maintain backend services that support Poshmark’s marketplace experience.\n\nCollaborate with peers and senior engineers to implement scalable, efficient, and maintainable systems.\n\nWrite clean, well-documented, and well-tested code following best practices.\n\nParticipate in code reviews and learn from feedback to continually improve.\n\nTroubleshoot and fix issues across distributed systems in production environments.\n\nContribute to improving development processes, tooling, and team workflows.\n\n6-Month Accomplishments:\n\nBecome proficient with Poshmark’s tech stack, development tools, and codebase.\n\nShip production-quality code with guidance from senior team members.\n\nTake ownership of small to medium-sized components or features.\n\nCollaborate effectively with Product, QA, and Design teams on feature delivery.\n\n12+ Month Accomplishments:\n\nIndependently deliver features from design to production.\n\nContribute to performance improvements and scalability initiatives.\n\nDevelop a strong understanding of Poshmark’s system architecture and make data-driven technical decisions.\n\nParticipate in technical discussions and contribute ideas to improve platform reliability and efficiency.\n\nMentor interns or new hires joining the team.\n\n\n\n\n💪 WHAT YOU’LL BRING\n\n2 - 4 years of professional experience (including internships) in backend software engineering.\n\nStrong understanding of computer science fundamentals — data structures, algorithms, and software design principles.\n\nProficiency in at least one backend language (e.g., Ruby, Java, Python, or Go).\n\nFamiliarity with RESTful APIs, databases (SQL/NoSQL), and caching or message-queue systems.\n\nInterest in cloud technologies (AWS, GCP, or similar) and scalable architectures.\n\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.\n\nCollaborative, curious, and motivated to learn and grow within a fast-paced environment.\n\n"},{"id":"b85cce7a-9349-46e2-954f-710db8ac0eb9","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Web","department":"All Departments","team":"Apps Team","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"US California (Redwood City) - Office","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-08T15:37:48.862+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Redwood City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/b85cce7a-9349-46e2-954f-710db8ac0eb9","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/b85cce7a-9349-46e2-954f-710db8ac0eb9/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Poshmark</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Poshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection.</strong> Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Poshmark is looking for a talented and creative <strong>Staff Web Engineer</strong>. The candidate is expected to create web applications that have a simple user interface and solid code that touches the lives of millions of users. The role will be dynamic and varied, requiring a versatile self-starter willing to dive into multiple initiatives. This role will provide an excellent opportunity to implement code that may run in production, at scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">While having the opportunity to work with a talented team to rapidly roll out changes and measure their impact, while being mentored and guided.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Responsible for creating web application features.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop a scalable, high performance and maintainable code.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with web technologies built on Web, database, and caching technologies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Tune the performance for the web application.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>6-Month Accomplishments</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Get familiar with the existing web architecture and code base.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Should be able to independently drive the feature development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have a good collaboration within the team. Also, with other teams like Product, Design, QA, devOps etc</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Should participate in technical discussions and be able to evaluate the design and architecture of the solution to the problems.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>12+ Month Accomplishments</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Come up with ideas/changes to improve the application both from performance and scalability perspective.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish yourself as technical lead for the web team.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Desired Skills</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8 years software development experience, including at least 3 years in building easy to use, responsive web applications</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in any of the following is highly desirable - Node, Vue, React, Angular, Ruby on Rails, NoSQL technologies (i.e. MongoDB), AWS.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Skills in building web development stack.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding and designing RESTful web services.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or a related field</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why Poshmark?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Poshmark is a leading social commerce platform for the next generation of retailers and shoppers. Through technology, our mission is to build the world’s most connected shopping experience, while empowering people to build thriving retail businesses. Since launching in 2011, Poshmark has become a vibrant social shopping community with seven million Seller Stylists helping 60 million users discover items they love from over 100 million listings. The company is backed by the world’s leading investment firms including <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://www.mayfield.com/\">Mayfield</a>, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://menlovc.com/\">Menlo Ventures</a>, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://www.ggvc.com/\">GGV Capital</a>, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://www.temasek.com.sg/\">Temasek</a>, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://inventuscap.com/\">Inventus Capital</a>, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://www.uncorkcapital.com/\">Uncork Capital</a>, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://ugvp.com/\">Union Grove Venture Partners</a>, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://www.jfshea.com/\">Shea Ventures</a> and <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://angel.co/\">AngelList</a>. For more information, please visit <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://www.poshmark.com\">www.poshmark.com</a>, or find us on <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.instagram.com/poshmark/\">Instagram</a>, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.facebook.com/Poshmark/\">Facebook</a>, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://twitter.com/poshmarkapp\">Twitter,</a> <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/poshmark/\">Pinterest</a> and <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/user/PoshmarkLIVE\">YouTube</a>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Poshmark, we’re constantly challenging the status quo and are looking for innovative and passionate people to help shape the future of Poshmark. We’re disrupting the industry by combining social connections with e-commerce through data-driven solutions and the latest technology to optimize our platform. We’re nothing without our amazing team who deliver an unparalleled social shopping experience to the millions of people we connect each day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We built Poshmark around four core values: 1) focus on people to create empowered communities that drive success; 2) together we grow to support each other to strive for our dreams; 3) lead with love to foster genuine connections built upon a foundation of respect; and 4) embrace your weirdness to accept and empower one another on their own unique journey. We’re invested in our team and community, working together to build an entirely new way to shop. That way, when we win, we all win together. Come help us build the most connected shopping experience ever.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Here’s what we’ll set you up with:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A team that is invested in your career growth and training</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive salary and equity, based on experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Company sponsors up to 100% cost for your health, dental and vision plans and up to 90% for your dependents</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work alongside world-class talent</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible vacation / paid time off policy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Parental leave</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Personal style encouraged (or not, whatever you’re in to)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Poshmark is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><br /></p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT POSHMARK\n\n\nPoshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection. Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.\n\n \n\nPoshmark is looking for a talented and creative Staff Web Engineer. The candidate is expected to create web applications that have a simple user interface and solid code that touches the lives of millions of users. The role will be dynamic and varied, requiring a versatile self-starter willing to dive into multiple initiatives. This role will provide an excellent opportunity to implement code that may run in production, at scale.\n\n\n\nWhile having the opportunity to work with a talented team to rapidly roll out changes and measure their impact, while being mentored and guided.\n\n\n\nResponsibilities\n\n - Responsible for creating web application features.\n\n - Develop a scalable, high performance and maintainable code.\n\n - Work with web technologies built on Web, database, and caching technologies.\n\n - Tune the performance for the web application.\n\n6-Month Accomplishments\n\n - Get familiar with the existing web architecture and code base.\n\n - Should be able to independently drive the feature development.\n\n - Have a good collaboration within the team. Also, with other teams like Product, Design, QA, devOps etc\n\n - Should participate in technical discussions and be able to evaluate the design and architecture of the solution to the problems.\n\n12+ Month Accomplishments\n\n - Come up with ideas/changes to improve the application both from performance and scalability perspective.\n\n - Establish yourself as technical lead for the web team.\n\nDesired Skills\n\n - 8 years software development experience, including at least 3 years in building easy to use, responsive web applications\n\n - Experience in any of the following is highly desirable - Node, Vue, React, Angular, Ruby on Rails, NoSQL technologies (i.e. MongoDB), AWS.\n\n - Skills in building web development stack.\n\n - Understanding and designing RESTful web services.\n\n - Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or a related field\n\nWhy Poshmark?\n\nPoshmark is a leading social commerce platform for the next generation of retailers and shoppers. Through technology, our mission is to build the world’s most connected shopping experience, while empowering people to build thriving retail businesses. Since launching in 2011, Poshmark has become a vibrant social shopping community with seven million Seller Stylists helping 60 million users discover items they love from over 100 million listings. The company is backed by the world’s leading investment firms including Mayfield http://www.mayfield.com/, Menlo Ventures https://menlovc.com/, GGV Capital http://www.ggvc.com/, Temasek http://www.temasek.com.sg/, Inventus Capital http://inventuscap.com/, Uncork Capital http://www.uncorkcapital.com/, Union Grove Venture Partners https://ugvp.com/, Shea Ventures http://www.jfshea.com/ and AngelList https://angel.co/. For more information, please visit www.poshmark.com http://www.poshmark.com, or find us on Instagram https://www.instagram.com/poshmark/, Facebook https://www.facebook.com/Poshmark/, Twitter, https://twitter.com/poshmarkapp Pinterest https://www.pinterest.com/poshmark/ and YouTube https://www.youtube.com/user/PoshmarkLIVE.\n\nAbout Us:\n\nAt Poshmark, we’re constantly challenging the status quo and are looking for innovative and passionate people to help shape the future of Poshmark. We’re disrupting the industry by combining social connections with e-commerce through data-driven solutions and the latest technology to optimize our platform. We’re nothing without our amazing team who deliver an unparalleled social shopping experience to the millions of people we connect each day.\n\nWe built Poshmark around four core values: 1) focus on people to create empowered communities that drive success; 2) together we grow to support each other to strive for our dreams; 3) lead with love to foster genuine connections built upon a foundation of respect; and 4) embrace your weirdness to accept and empower one another on their own unique journey. We’re invested in our team and community, working together to build an entirely new way to shop. That way, when we win, we all win together. Come help us build the most connected shopping experience ever.\n\nHere’s what we’ll set you up with:\n\n - A team that is invested in your career growth and training\n\n - Competitive salary and equity, based on experience\n\n - Company sponsors up to 100% cost for your health, dental and vision plans and up to 90% for your dependents\n\n - Work alongside world-class talent\n\n - Flexible vacation / paid time off policy\n\n - Parental leave\n\n - Personal style encouraged (or not, whatever you’re in to)\n\nPoshmark is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees.\n\n\n\n"},{"id":"461a37db-d133-4947-a17d-8afd2092a6fc","title":"Senior Software Engineer II, Machine Learning","department":"All Departments","team":"AI/ML Team","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"IN Tamil Nadu (Chennai) - Office","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-25T03:43:08.947+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"India","addressLocality":"Chennai"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/461a37db-d133-4947-a17d-8afd2092a6fc","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/461a37db-d133-4947-a17d-8afd2092a6fc/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Poshmark</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Poshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection.</strong> Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h1>Senior Machine Learning Engineer</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Poshmark is a leading social marketplace for new and secondhand styles for women, men, kids, home, and more. By combining the human connection of physical shopping with the scale, ease, and selection benefits of ecommerce, Poshmark makes buying and selling simple, social, and fun.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Machine Learning team is a central player in the Poshmark organization. Our mission is to build a world-class machine learning platform to bring value out of data for us and for our customers. Our goal is to democratize data science and machine learning, support exploding business, and use machine learning to drive value across the chain (Search, personalization, fraud detection, catalog digitisation to name a few)</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage the entire ML lifecycle from data collection to deployment and monitoring</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate across teams such as DS, QA, Infra and other engineering teams to productionize ML models</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write and optimize code for production environments, ensuring the robustness and reliability of ML services at scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage and support current solutions while evolving them to incorporate newer technologies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written, verbal, and presentation skills, with the ability to convey complex concepts in a clear and simple manner</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay updated with the latest developments in data science and machine learning</p></li></ul><h2>Desired Skills &amp; Experience</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of experience applying Machine Learning to concrete problems at large scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelors or Masters in Computer Science, Statistics, or related field</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong CS fundamentals. Should be able to write algorithms with ease.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid understanding of Data Science and ML fundamentals – Regression, Classification, Tree-based approach, Neural network, and sequence-based models.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working experience with at least one ML model: LLMs, GNN, Deep Learning, Logistic Regression, Gradient Boosting trees, etc.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Should have excellent understanding of ML lifecycle</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good understanding of system architecture. Have knowledge of big data technologies – streaming architecture, data pipelines, etc.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Python, SQL, Java or Scala</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good to have:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Big data systems – Spark, EMR, S3, AirFlow</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Production experience with LLMs and prompt engineering</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Flask, FastAPI, RabbitMQ, Embeddings and Vector DBs</p></li></ul></li></ul><h2>Our Techstack</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Pytorch, Tensorflow, Sklearn</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flask, Fastapi, Gunicorn, Quarkus</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">MLFlow, Sagemaker, Kibana, Airflow, Databricks, Grafana, Datadog</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Docker, Kubernetes, Jenkins</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Redis, Redshift, MongoDB, Spark, Kafka, RabbitMQ, Milvus</p></li></ul><h2>Why Poshmark?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Poshmark is a leading social marketplace for new and secondhand style for women, men, kids, pets, home, and more. By combining the human connection of physical shopping with the scale, ease, and selection benefits of ecommerce, Poshmark makes buying and selling simple, social, and sustainable. Its community of more than 70 million registered users across the U.S., Canada, and Australia is driving the future of commerce while promoting more sustainable consumption. For more information, please visit <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://www.poshmark.com\">www.poshmark.com</a>, and for company news and announcements, please visit <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://investors.poshmark.com\">investors.poshmark.com</a>. You can also find Poshmark on Instagram, Facebook, Twitter, Pinterest, and YouTube.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>About Us</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Poshmark, we’re constantly challenging the status quo and are looking for innovative and passionate people to help shape the future of Poshmark. We’re disrupting the industry by combining social connections with e-commerce through data-driven solutions and the latest technology to optimize our platform. We’re nothing without our amazing team who deliver an unparalleled social shopping experience to the millions of people we connect each day.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We built Poshmark around four core values:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Focus on People to create empowered communities that drive success;</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Together we Grow to support each other to strive for our dreams;</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead with Love to foster genuine connections built upon a foundation of respect; and</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Embrace your Weirdness to accept and empower one another on their own unique journey.</p></li></ol><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re invested in our team and community, working together to build an entirely new way to shop. That way, when we win, we all win together. Come help us build the most connected shopping experience ever.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT POSHMARK\n\n\nPoshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection. Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.\n\n \n\n\nSENIOR MACHINE LEARNING ENGINEER\n\nPoshmark is a leading social marketplace for new and secondhand styles for women, men, kids, home, and more. By combining the human connection of physical shopping with the scale, ease, and selection benefits of ecommerce, Poshmark makes buying and selling simple, social, and fun.\n\n\n\nThe Machine Learning team is a central player in the Poshmark organization. Our mission is to build a world-class machine learning platform to bring value out of data for us and for our customers. Our goal is to democratize data science and machine learning, support exploding business, and use machine learning to drive value across the chain (Search, personalization, fraud detection, catalog digitisation to name a few)\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Manage the entire ML lifecycle from data collection to deployment and monitoring\n\n - Collaborate across teams such as DS, QA, Infra and other engineering teams to productionize ML models\n\n - Write and optimize code for production environments, ensuring the robustness and reliability of ML services at scale\n\n - Manage and support current solutions while evolving them to incorporate newer technologies\n\n - Strong written, verbal, and presentation skills, with the ability to convey complex concepts in a clear and simple manner\n\n - Stay updated with the latest developments in data science and machine learning\n\n\nDESIRED SKILLS & EXPERIENCE\n\n - 4+ years of experience applying Machine Learning to concrete problems at large scale\n\n - Bachelors or Masters in Computer Science, Statistics, or related field\n\n - Strong CS fundamentals. Should be able to write algorithms with ease.\n\n - Solid understanding of Data Science and ML fundamentals – Regression, Classification, Tree-based approach, Neural network, and sequence-based models.\n\n - Working experience with at least one ML model: LLMs, GNN, Deep Learning, Logistic Regression, Gradient Boosting trees, etc.\n\n - Should have excellent understanding of ML lifecycle\n\n - Good understanding of system architecture. Have knowledge of big data technologies – streaming architecture, data pipelines, etc.\n\n - Experience with Python, SQL, Java or Scala\n\n - Good to have:\n   \n   - Big data systems – Spark, EMR, S3, AirFlow\n   \n   - Production experience with LLMs and prompt engineering\n   \n   - Experience with Flask, FastAPI, RabbitMQ, Embeddings and Vector DBs\n\n\nOUR TECHSTACK\n\n - Pytorch, Tensorflow, Sklearn\n\n - Flask, Fastapi, Gunicorn, Quarkus\n\n - MLFlow, Sagemaker, Kibana, Airflow, Databricks, Grafana, Datadog\n\n - Docker, Kubernetes, Jenkins\n\n - Redis, Redshift, MongoDB, Spark, Kafka, RabbitMQ, Milvus\n\n\nWHY POSHMARK?\n\nPoshmark is a leading social marketplace for new and secondhand style for women, men, kids, pets, home, and more. By combining the human connection of physical shopping with the scale, ease, and selection benefits of ecommerce, Poshmark makes buying and selling simple, social, and sustainable. Its community of more than 70 million registered users across the U.S., Canada, and Australia is driving the future of commerce while promoting more sustainable consumption. For more information, please visit www.poshmark.com http://www.poshmark.com, and for company news and announcements, please visit investors.poshmark.com http://investors.poshmark.com. You can also find Poshmark on Instagram, Facebook, Twitter, Pinterest, and YouTube.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT US\n\nAt Poshmark, we’re constantly challenging the status quo and are looking for innovative and passionate people to help shape the future of Poshmark. We’re disrupting the industry by combining social connections with e-commerce through data-driven solutions and the latest technology to optimize our platform. We’re nothing without our amazing team who deliver an unparalleled social shopping experience to the millions of people we connect each day.\n\n\n\nWe built Poshmark around four core values:\n\n\n\n 1. Focus on People to create empowered communities that drive success;\n\n 2. Together we Grow to support each other to strive for our dreams;\n\n 3. Lead with Love to foster genuine connections built upon a foundation of respect; and\n\n 4. Embrace your Weirdness to accept and empower one another on their own unique journey.\n\n\n\nWe’re invested in our team and community, working together to build an entirely new way to shop. That way, when we win, we all win together. Come help us build the most connected shopping experience ever.\n\n\n"},{"id":"62cbe59f-9ef5-454f-9987-4c537a050984","title":"Sr. Software Engineer II, Web","department":"All Departments","team":"Apps Team","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"US California (Redwood City) - Office","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-02-11T18:52:41.175+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Redwood City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/62cbe59f-9ef5-454f-9987-4c537a050984","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/62cbe59f-9ef5-454f-9987-4c537a050984/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Poshmark</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Poshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection.</strong> Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Poshmark is looking for a <strong>Senior Web Engineer II</strong> to join our Buyer Pod. We are the team responsible for the core user journey: feed, discovery, search, and listing details. We don’t just build interfaces; we build the engine that helps millions of users find and buy what they love.<br />We are looking for an engineer who values the \"how\" as much as the \"what.\" You should be someone who understands the browser’s rendering pipeline and DOM underpinnings deeply, ensuring that our migration from Vue 2 to Vue 3 is not just a version bump, but a leap forward in performance and code quality.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Core Responsibilities</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Architect &amp; Execute:</strong> Lead small engineering pods to take complex features from discovery to production-scale delivery.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Vue Migration:</strong> Act as a key driver in our transition from Vue 2 to Vue 3, leveraging the Composition API and modern build tools (Vite/Webpack).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>High-Performance UI:</strong> Build responsive, accessible, and high-performance web applications with a focus on Core Web Vitals and efficient state management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Design Partnership:</strong> Collaborate closely with Product and Design to ensure every pixel serves the user experience. You should bring a strong \"sense of taste\" to everything you build.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical Mentorship:</strong> Influence the technical roadmap and mentor junior/mid-level engineers through code reviews and architecture discussions.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">90-Day Success Metrics</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Immediate Impact:</strong> Contribute production-ready code to both our legacy and modern environments within your first 30 days.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Migration Milestone:</strong> Successfully migrate a complex module or shared component from Vue 2 to Vue 3.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Feature Ownership:</strong> Lead the technical execution of a new buyer-facing feature, ensuring it meets our standards for performance and design polish.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12-Month Success Metrics</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Architecture Evolution:</strong> Propose and implement structural improvements to our web stack that measurably improve developer velocity and site speed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>System Expert:</strong> Become the primary technical point of contact for our search and discovery front-end architecture.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Team Growth:</strong> Level up the team’s collective knowledge of browser internals and modern JavaScript best practices.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Desired Skills</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>5+ years of software development experience</strong>, with a focus on high-scale web applications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Under the Hood Knowledge:</strong> Deep understanding of JavaScript fundamentals (Event Loop, DOM API, browser rendering) beyond framework-specific abstractions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Vue Specialist:</strong> Proven experience with <strong>Vue 2 and Vue 3</strong>. Experience navigating the friction of migrating between the two is highly preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Leadership:</strong> Experience leading small teams or project \"pods\" and a track record of driving features to completion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Product Intuition:</strong> A sharp eye for UI/UX and a passion for creating \"great\" web design rather than just \"functional\" code.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Stack:</strong> Familiarity with modern build tools (Vite, Webpack), RESTful APIs, and distributed systems.</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT POSHMARK\n\n\nPoshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection. Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.\n\n \n\nPoshmark is looking for a Senior Web Engineer II to join our Buyer Pod. We are the team responsible for the core user journey: feed, discovery, search, and listing details. We don’t just build interfaces; we build the engine that helps millions of users find and buy what they love.\nWe are looking for an engineer who values the \"how\" as much as the \"what.\" You should be someone who understands the browser’s rendering pipeline and DOM underpinnings deeply, ensuring that our migration from Vue 2 to Vue 3 is not just a version bump, but a leap forward in performance and code quality.\n\n\nCore Responsibilities\n\n - Architect & Execute: Lead small engineering pods to take complex features from discovery to production-scale delivery.\n\n - The Vue Migration: Act as a key driver in our transition from Vue 2 to Vue 3, leveraging the Composition API and modern build tools (Vite/Webpack).\n\n - High-Performance UI: Build responsive, accessible, and high-performance web applications with a focus on Core Web Vitals and efficient state management.\n\n - Design Partnership: Collaborate closely with Product and Design to ensure every pixel serves the user experience. You should bring a strong \"sense of taste\" to everything you build.\n\n - Technical Mentorship: Influence the technical roadmap and mentor junior/mid-level engineers through code reviews and architecture discussions.\n\n90-Day Success Metrics\n\n - Immediate Impact: Contribute production-ready code to both our legacy and modern environments within your first 30 days.\n\n - Migration Milestone: Successfully migrate a complex module or shared component from Vue 2 to Vue 3.\n\n - Feature Ownership: Lead the technical execution of a new buyer-facing feature, ensuring it meets our standards for performance and design polish.\n\n12-Month Success Metrics\n\n - Architecture Evolution: Propose and implement structural improvements to our web stack that measurably improve developer velocity and site speed.\n\n - System Expert: Become the primary technical point of contact for our search and discovery front-end architecture.\n\n - Team Growth: Level up the team’s collective knowledge of browser internals and modern JavaScript best practices.\n\nDesired Skills\n\n - 5+ years of software development experience, with a focus on high-scale web applications.\n\n - Under the Hood Knowledge: Deep understanding of JavaScript fundamentals (Event Loop, DOM API, browser rendering) beyond framework-specific abstractions.\n\n - Vue Specialist: Proven experience with Vue 2 and Vue 3. Experience navigating the friction of migrating between the two is highly preferred.\n\n - Leadership: Experience leading small teams or project \"pods\" and a track record of driving features to completion.\n\n - Product Intuition: A sharp eye for UI/UX and a passion for creating \"great\" web design rather than just \"functional\" code.\n\n - The Stack: Familiarity with modern build tools (Vite, Webpack), RESTful APIs, and distributed systems."},{"id":"58c2af50-fb51-4c76-80fd-67d0c5b489b3","title":"Staff Growth Product Manager","department":"All Departments","team":"Product Management Team","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"US California (Redwood City) - Office","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-04-09T21:27:01.911+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Redwood City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/58c2af50-fb51-4c76-80fd-67d0c5b489b3","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/58c2af50-fb51-4c76-80fd-67d0c5b489b3/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Poshmark</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Poshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection.</strong> Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Poshmark is seeking a Staff Growth Product Manager to drive high-impact, data-informed growth across the marketplace. This role will initially focus on new user onboarding and early lifecycle experiences, with the opportunity to expand into broader growth opportunities over time, including engagement, retention, and monetization.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will be responsible for identifying and scaling the highest leverage growth opportunities across the user journey. This includes optimizing first touch experiences, accelerating activation, and improving long-term retention. Over time, you will flex across surfaces and problems as priorities evolve.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is for a builder who thrives in ambiguity, brings strong analytical rigor, and takes full ownership of outcomes from problem definition through execution.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Responsibilities:</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and improve key growth funnels across the user lifecycle, with an initial focus on new user onboarding and early activation for buyers and sellers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify and prioritize high-impact growth opportunities using quantitative analysis, user research, and experimentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead a high-velocity experimentation program across onboarding, discovery, engagement, and retention surfaces</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and analyze experiments with strong statistical rigor, and translate results into clear product decisions and roadmap direction</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct and synthesize user research to understand motivations, behaviors, and drop-off drivers across the funnel</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Apply principles of customer psychology, habit formation, and behavioral economics to inform product design and optimization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and maintain core growth metrics, dashboards, and KPI frameworks to ensure visibility and alignment across teams</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with design, engineering, data, and marketing to deliver high-quality, scalable growth initiatives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate strategy, insights, and trade-offs clearly to senior leadership with a focus on business impact</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate roadmap strategy, experiment results, and investment trade-offs to senior leadership with precise business impact framing, clear assumptions, and well-reasoned recommendations.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6-Month Accomplishments:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Audit the new user journey for buyers and sellers, identifying key friction points and opportunities through data and research</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish a clear activation framework, including key metrics, instrumentation, and shared dashboards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Launch and iterate on experiments targeting the highest impact onboarding and activation gaps</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define activation milestones and outline a roadmap to reduce time to value</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">12+ Month Accomplishments:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deliver measurable improvements in key growth metrics, including activation, retention, and engagement across the user lifecycle</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expand ownership beyond onboarding to additional growth surfaces such as discovery, re-engagement, and monetization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish a consistent experimentation engine with a strong pipeline of ideas and documented learnings</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve time to key user actions such as first listing, first purchase, and first offer</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and socialize a growth playbook including frameworks, metrics, and best practices adopted across the organization</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Required Qualifications</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6–10 years of experience in product management, with a significant portion dedicated to growth-specific functions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record of driving product-led growth in a consumer or marketplace environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical skills with experience in experimentation, funnel analysis, and data-driven decision making</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to operate across a wide range of problem spaces, from onboarding to retention and beyond</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience applying user research and behavioral insights to product design</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills with the ability to influence cross-functional stakeholders and senior leadership</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High ownership mindset with the ability to operate effectively in ambiguous, fast-paced environments</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT POSHMARK\n\n\nPoshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection. Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.\n\n \n\n\n\nPoshmark is seeking a Staff Growth Product Manager to drive high-impact, data-informed growth across the marketplace. This role will initially focus on new user onboarding and early lifecycle experiences, with the opportunity to expand into broader growth opportunities over time, including engagement, retention, and monetization.\n\n\n\nYou will be responsible for identifying and scaling the highest leverage growth opportunities across the user journey. This includes optimizing first touch experiences, accelerating activation, and improving long-term retention. Over time, you will flex across surfaces and problems as priorities evolve.\n\n\n\nThis role is for a builder who thrives in ambiguity, brings strong analytical rigor, and takes full ownership of outcomes from problem definition through execution.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES:\n\n\n\n - Own and improve key growth funnels across the user lifecycle, with an initial focus on new user onboarding and early activation for buyers and sellers\n\n - Identify and prioritize high-impact growth opportunities using quantitative analysis, user research, and experimentation\n\n - Lead a high-velocity experimentation program across onboarding, discovery, engagement, and retention surfaces\n\n - Design and analyze experiments with strong statistical rigor, and translate results into clear product decisions and roadmap direction\n\n - Conduct and synthesize user research to understand motivations, behaviors, and drop-off drivers across the funnel\n\n - Apply principles of customer psychology, habit formation, and behavioral economics to inform product design and optimization\n\n - Define and maintain core growth metrics, dashboards, and KPI frameworks to ensure visibility and alignment across teams\n\n - Partner closely with design, engineering, data, and marketing to deliver high-quality, scalable growth initiatives\n\n - Communicate strategy, insights, and trade-offs clearly to senior leadership with a focus on business impact\n\n - Communicate roadmap strategy, experiment results, and investment trade-offs to senior leadership with precise business impact framing, clear assumptions, and well-reasoned recommendations.\n\n\n\n6-Month Accomplishments:\n\n - Audit the new user journey for buyers and sellers, identifying key friction points and opportunities through data and research\n\n - Establish a clear activation framework, including key metrics, instrumentation, and shared dashboards\n\n - Launch and iterate on experiments targeting the highest impact onboarding and activation gaps\n\n - Define activation milestones and outline a roadmap to reduce time to value\n\n\n\n12+ Month Accomplishments:\n\n\n\n - Deliver measurable improvements in key growth metrics, including activation, retention, and engagement across the user lifecycle\n\n - Expand ownership beyond onboarding to additional growth surfaces such as discovery, re-engagement, and monetization\n\n - Establish a consistent experimentation engine with a strong pipeline of ideas and documented learnings\n\n - Improve time to key user actions such as first listing, first purchase, and first offer\n\n - Develop and socialize a growth playbook including frameworks, metrics, and best practices adopted across the organization\n\n\n\n\nREQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS\n\n\n\n - 6–10 years of experience in product management, with a significant portion dedicated to growth-specific functions.\n\n - Proven track record of driving product-led growth in a consumer or marketplace environment\n\n - Strong analytical skills with experience in experimentation, funnel analysis, and data-driven decision making\n\n - Ability to operate across a wide range of problem spaces, from onboarding to retention and beyond\n\n - Experience applying user research and behavioral insights to product design\n\n - Excellent communication skills with the ability to influence cross-functional stakeholders and senior leadership\n\n - High ownership mindset with the ability to operate effectively in ambiguous, fast-paced environments"},{"id":"dd52fc91-8db4-4f59-bf17-f9d1c04dd010","title":"Manager, Digital Design","department":"All Departments","team":"Revenue Team","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"US California (Redwood City) - Office","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-13T01:41:15.314+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Redwood City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/dd52fc91-8db4-4f59-bf17-f9d1c04dd010","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/dd52fc91-8db4-4f59-bf17-f9d1c04dd010/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Poshmark</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Poshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection.</strong> Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for a Manager, Art &amp; Design Direction to lead the visual expression of our brand across content, campaigns, and digital experiences. This is a player-coach role for someone with exceptional taste, a strong design point of view, and the ability to execute at a high level while managing and mentoring a small team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Manager, Art &amp; Design Direction, you will sit at the intersection of brand and content, shaping how Poshmark shows up visually across every touchpoint — from social and editorial to campaigns and brand moments.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll partner closely with the Fashion &amp; Creative Director to translate strategic vision into compelling visual execution, while setting the day-to-day creative standard for your team. This role requires someone who can move seamlessly from concept to execution — equally comfortable building a campaign mood board as they are working in Figma or AI-assisted design tools to bring ideas to life.  Will be responsible managing all creative projects for the Revenue team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h2><h3><strong>Creative Direction &amp; Visual Execution</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the visual direction for brand and creative content initiatives, from concept through final delivery</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and maintain a cohesive visual language across all channels — social, campaigns, editorial, digital, and marketing collateral</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Concept and produce high-quality visual assets that reflect Poshmark’s brand and resonate with our community</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bring a fashion-forward, culturally relevant perspective to all creative work, staying ahead of trends in fashion, retail, and visual culture</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Team Leadership</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage and mentor a small team of creatives (designers and copywriter), providing clear, actionable feedback</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prioritize and allocate work across the team, balancing creative quality with timelines and business needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Foster a culture of craft, curiosity, and high creative standards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with the Creative &amp; Fashion Director to align on vision and escalate key creative decisions</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Project &amp; Production Management</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the end-to-end creative production process: briefing, concepting, execution, review, and delivery</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage multiple projects simultaneously with strong organizational rigor (timelines, asset tracking, stakeholder reviews)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally with Marketing, Product Marketing, Growth, Partnerships, and other teams to deliver impactful creative</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure all deliverables are on-brand, on-time, and meet a high quality bar</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Tools, Asset Management &amp; Creative Operations</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay current on emerging design tools, AI-assisted creative workflows, and new platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Introduce new processes and efficiencies without compromising creative quality</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Champion the use of best-in-class tools across the creative workflow</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and maintain the shared creative file system, including:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Folder structure and organization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Naming conventions and version control</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Access management across teams</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish and enforce standards to ensure creative assets are scalable, accessible, and easy to use across the organization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as the central point of coordination for creative assets, ensuring seamless collaboration across Brand, Marketing, and cross-functional teams</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></h2><h3><strong>Creative &amp; Design</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5–8 years of experience in art direction, design, or creative content, ideally within fashion, e-commerce, or consumer brands</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong portfolio demonstrating exceptional taste across typography, color, composition, and visual storytelling</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience directing and producing both still and motion content (photo, video, social, campaign)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep interest in fashion, style, and visual culture</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Technical Skills</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expert proficiency in Adobe Creative Suite (Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign, Premiere)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong working knowledge of Figma and design systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with AI-powered creative tools (e.g., Midjourney, Adobe Firefly, RunwayML, or similar)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing across digital formats: social, web, email, and digital OOH</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Leadership &amp; Management</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing or leading creative teams, formally or in a project leadership capacity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communicator who can provide clear, constructive creative direction</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to balance hands-on creative work with team leadership responsibilities</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Project Management</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Highly organized with experience managing multiple projects across stakeholders and timelines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable using project management tools (e.g., Asana, Monday, Notion)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to scope work, anticipate risks, and keep projects moving efficiently</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bonus Points</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background or strong interest in resale, secondhand fashion, or the creator economy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with influencer or creator content workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with performance-driven or growth marketing creative</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>Why Join Poshmark?</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll play a key role in shaping the visual identity of a brand at the intersection of fashion, technology, and community. This is an opportunity to lead creative work that reaches millions of users while building a modern, scalable, and culturally relevant design function.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT POSHMARK\n\n\nPoshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection. Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.\n\n \n\nWe’re looking for a Manager, Art & Design Direction to lead the visual expression of our brand across content, campaigns, and digital experiences. This is a player-coach role for someone with exceptional taste, a strong design point of view, and the ability to execute at a high level while managing and mentoring a small team.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAs Manager, Art & Design Direction, you will sit at the intersection of brand and content, shaping how Poshmark shows up visually across every touchpoint — from social and editorial to campaigns and brand moments.\n\nYou’ll partner closely with the Fashion & Creative Director to translate strategic vision into compelling visual execution, while setting the day-to-day creative standard for your team. This role requires someone who can move seamlessly from concept to execution — equally comfortable building a campaign mood board as they are working in Figma or AI-assisted design tools to bring ideas to life.  Will be responsible managing all creative projects for the Revenue team.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n\nCREATIVE DIRECTION & VISUAL EXECUTION\n\n - Own the visual direction for brand and creative content initiatives, from concept through final delivery\n\n - Develop and maintain a cohesive visual language across all channels — social, campaigns, editorial, digital, and marketing collateral\n\n - Concept and produce high-quality visual assets that reflect Poshmark’s brand and resonate with our community\n\n - Bring a fashion-forward, culturally relevant perspective to all creative work, staying ahead of trends in fashion, retail, and visual culture\n\n\nTEAM LEADERSHIP\n\n - Manage and mentor a small team of creatives (designers and copywriter), providing clear, actionable feedback\n\n - Prioritize and allocate work across the team, balancing creative quality with timelines and business needs\n\n - Foster a culture of craft, curiosity, and high creative standards\n\n - Partner closely with the Creative & Fashion Director to align on vision and escalate key creative decisions\n\n\nPROJECT & PRODUCTION MANAGEMENT\n\n - Own the end-to-end creative production process: briefing, concepting, execution, review, and delivery\n\n - Manage multiple projects simultaneously with strong organizational rigor (timelines, asset tracking, stakeholder reviews)\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally with Marketing, Product Marketing, Growth, Partnerships, and other teams to deliver impactful creative\n\n - Ensure all deliverables are on-brand, on-time, and meet a high quality bar\n\n\nTOOLS, ASSET MANAGEMENT & CREATIVE OPERATIONS\n\n - Stay current on emerging design tools, AI-assisted creative workflows, and new platforms\n\n - Introduce new processes and efficiencies without compromising creative quality\n\n - Champion the use of best-in-class tools across the creative workflow\n\n - Own and maintain the shared creative file system, including:\n   \n   - Folder structure and organization\n   \n   - Naming conventions and version control\n   \n   - Access management across teams\n\n - Establish and enforce standards to ensure creative assets are scalable, accessible, and easy to use across the organization\n\n - Serve as the central point of coordination for creative assets, ensuring seamless collaboration across Brand, Marketing, and cross-functional teams\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE’RE LOOKING FOR\n\n\nCREATIVE & DESIGN\n\n - 5–8 years of experience in art direction, design, or creative content, ideally within fashion, e-commerce, or consumer brands\n\n - A strong portfolio demonstrating exceptional taste across typography, color, composition, and visual storytelling\n\n - Experience directing and producing both still and motion content (photo, video, social, campaign)\n\n - Deep interest in fashion, style, and visual culture\n\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\n\n - Expert proficiency in Adobe Creative Suite (Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign, Premiere)\n\n - Strong working knowledge of Figma and design systems\n\n - Familiarity with AI-powered creative tools (e.g., Midjourney, Adobe Firefly, RunwayML, or similar)\n\n - Experience designing across digital formats: social, web, email, and digital OOH\n\nLeadership & Management\n\n - Experience managing or leading creative teams, formally or in a project leadership capacity\n\n - Strong communicator who can provide clear, constructive creative direction\n\n - Ability to balance hands-on creative work with team leadership responsibilities\n\nProject Management\n\n - Highly organized with experience managing multiple projects across stakeholders and timelines\n\n - Comfortable using project management tools (e.g., Asana, Monday, Notion)\n\n - Ability to scope work, anticipate risks, and keep projects moving efficiently\n\nBonus Points\n\n - Background or strong interest in resale, secondhand fashion, or the creator economy\n\n - Experience working with influencer or creator content workflows\n\n - Familiarity with performance-driven or growth marketing creative\n\n \n\n\nWHY JOIN POSHMARK?\n\nYou’ll play a key role in shaping the visual identity of a brand at the intersection of fashion, technology, and community. This is an opportunity to lead creative work that reaches millions of users while building a modern, scalable, and culturally relevant design function."},{"id":"c058d95f-99d3-4998-abc8-3e656a7c328b","title":"Director of Product Design ","department":"All Departments","team":"Product Design Team","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"US California (Redwood City) - Office","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-27T23:58:30.202+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Redwood City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/c058d95f-99d3-4998-abc8-3e656a7c328b","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/c058d95f-99d3-4998-abc8-3e656a7c328b/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Poshmark</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Poshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection.</strong> Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h1><strong>Role Overview</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Poshmark is seeking a <strong>Director of Product Design</strong> to lead and elevate our end-to-end product design experience. This role will define how users discover, buy, interact and sell across our platform, shaping a seamless and engaging journey for both sides of our marketplace.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a key member of the product leadership team, you will report to the Chief Product Officer and set the design vision, guide a talented team of designers and managers, and partner closely with Product, Engineering, Customer Research, Analytics and Marketing to deliver thoughtful, high-impact experiences. This role requires a balance of <strong>strategic leadership, strong design craft, prior working experience utilizing AI-based design tools, and deep understanding of marketplace ecosystems</strong>.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Design Vision &amp; Strategy</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and drive a cohesive, forward-looking design vision across Poshmark’s buyer and seller experiences ensuring that Poshmark’s product stays current with evolving design systems and industry trends.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify, socialize and utilize customer needs across the marketplace for both shoppers and sellers as an input to prioritize and develop a perspective on design priorities and decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Align design strategy with company goals, ensuring meaningful impact on engagement, growth, and retention</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Champion design as a strategic partner in shaping the product roadmap</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner strategically with engineering to ensure great understanding &amp; execution of our design thinking</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Team Leadership &amp; Development</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead, mentor, and scale a high-performing design organization, including career and skills development for designers at every level including managing managers, and mentoring junior designers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build a structured career ladder and path for our designers at all levels of their careers from junior individual designers to senior managers and set clear expectations and a culture of evolution and growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish clear design principles, systems, and processes to ensure consistency and quality</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Foster a culture of excellence, inclusivity, and continuous growth</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Marketplace Design</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Oversee design for core marketplace journeys, including discovery, listing, selling, social interaction, and transactions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design for a two-sided ecosystem, balancing the needs of shoppers and sellers to improve liquidity, trust, and overall marketplace health</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive innovation in social commerce experiences, including feeds, sharing, and community engagement</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Execution &amp; Craft Excellence</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Oversee design for the overall marketplace and core customer journeys. Maintain a high bar for design quality and innovation across customer journeys, and ensure smart alignment across mobile and web platforms.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Utilize design as a means to drive innovation in social experiences including community features</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide hands-on direction through critiques, reviews, and selective individual contribution for new exploratory workstreams that require further review and refinement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leverage customer insights derived from a combination of user feedback, research and quantitative data to inform and validate design priorities, decisions, and evaluate impact</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead design execution, design systems, and operations across the product roadmap—owning intake, prioritization, and resourcing to ensure design is embedded in planning and focused on highest-impact work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and scale clear systems for scoping, assigning, and reviewing work across a global, distributed design team, with strong visibility into portfolio priorities</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI Transformation</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead the design team's transition to AI-powered workflows including systematic change in how the team prototypes, iterates, and ships</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with product and engineering on AI-native development models where design, PM, and eng are iterating together in real time rather than passing work sequentially</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use AI to extend design capacity and speed without sacrificing quality</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Cross-Functional Leadership</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Product and Engineering leaders to define strategy and deliver impactful outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with Brand, Creative and Marketing to ensure a cohesive, end-to-end user experience and that we deliver on a shared brand and product vision for Poshmark</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Engineering to translate design systems into implementation standards, ensuring consistency across feature development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate design decisions clearly and influence stakeholders at all levels</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with team members who will report into you, and coordinate design work with you, from our India and Korea offices.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h1><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At least 10–15+ years of experience in product or UX design, with a significant portion in leadership roles</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven success building, managing, and scaling design teams, including managing managers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing for marketplaces, e-commerce, or social platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on familiarity with marketplace dynamics, either professionally or as an active participant</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Design &amp; Product Expertise</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong portfolio demonstrating high-quality, user-centered design at scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep expertise in mobile-first consumer products and complex, multi-sided systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong systems thinking and ability to design for both detail and scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience using AI design tools like Figma Make or Claude Design</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good familiarity with experimentation, growth design, and data-informed decision-making</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Leadership &amp; Influence</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strategic mindset with the ability to connect design decisions to business outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional communication and storytelling skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to influence cross-functional partners and senior leadership</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience deploying and driving scale of design work and prototyping through use of AI-based design tools</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Marketplace Insight &amp; User Empathy</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of marketplace dynamics, including supply/demand balance, trust, and incentives</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Empathy for diverse user segments, from casual participants to power sellers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passion for community-driven, social product experiences</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h1><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with live commerce, creator tools, or social engagement features</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background or experience with two-sided marketplaces, fashion, retail, resale, or lifestyle marketplaces</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h1><strong>Why Join Poshmark</strong></h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Shape the future of social commerce at scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead design for a deeply engaged, entrepreneurial community</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build experiences that directly impact users’ livelihoods and success</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work alongside a collaborative, mission-driven team</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT POSHMARK\n\n\nPoshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection. Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.\n\n \n\n\nROLE OVERVIEW\n\nPoshmark is seeking a Director of Product Design to lead and elevate our end-to-end product design experience. This role will define how users discover, buy, interact and sell across our platform, shaping a seamless and engaging journey for both sides of our marketplace.\n\nAs a key member of the product leadership team, you will report to the Chief Product Officer and set the design vision, guide a talented team of designers and managers, and partner closely with Product, Engineering, Customer Research, Analytics and Marketing to deliver thoughtful, high-impact experiences. This role requires a balance of strategic leadership, strong design craft, prior working experience utilizing AI-based design tools, and deep understanding of marketplace ecosystems.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\nDesign Vision & Strategy\n\n - Define and drive a cohesive, forward-looking design vision across Poshmark’s buyer and seller experiences ensuring that Poshmark’s product stays current with evolving design systems and industry trends.\n\n - Identify, socialize and utilize customer needs across the marketplace for both shoppers and sellers as an input to prioritize and develop a perspective on design priorities and decisions.\n\n - Align design strategy with company goals, ensuring meaningful impact on engagement, growth, and retention\n\n - Champion design as a strategic partner in shaping the product roadmap\n\n - Partner strategically with engineering to ensure great understanding & execution of our design thinking\n\nTeam Leadership & Development\n\n - Lead, mentor, and scale a high-performing design organization, including career and skills development for designers at every level including managing managers, and mentoring junior designers.\n\n - Build a structured career ladder and path for our designers at all levels of their careers from junior individual designers to senior managers and set clear expectations and a culture of evolution and growth.\n\n - Establish clear design principles, systems, and processes to ensure consistency and quality\n\n - Foster a culture of excellence, inclusivity, and continuous growth\n\nMarketplace Design\n\n - Oversee design for core marketplace journeys, including discovery, listing, selling, social interaction, and transactions\n\n - Design for a two-sided ecosystem, balancing the needs of shoppers and sellers to improve liquidity, trust, and overall marketplace health\n\n - Drive innovation in social commerce experiences, including feeds, sharing, and community engagement\n\nExecution & Craft Excellence\n\n - Oversee design for the overall marketplace and core customer journeys. Maintain a high bar for design quality and innovation across customer journeys, and ensure smart alignment across mobile and web platforms.\n\n - Utilize design as a means to drive innovation in social experiences including community features\n\n - Provide hands-on direction through critiques, reviews, and selective individual contribution for new exploratory workstreams that require further review and refinement\n\n - Leverage customer insights derived from a combination of user feedback, research and quantitative data to inform and validate design priorities, decisions, and evaluate impact\n\n - Lead design execution, design systems, and operations across the product roadmap—owning intake, prioritization, and resourcing to ensure design is embedded in planning and focused on highest-impact work.\n\n - Build and scale clear systems for scoping, assigning, and reviewing work across a global, distributed design team, with strong visibility into portfolio priorities\n\nAI Transformation\n\n - Lead the design team's transition to AI-powered workflows including systematic change in how the team prototypes, iterates, and ships\n\n - Partner with product and engineering on AI-native development models where design, PM, and eng are iterating together in real time rather than passing work sequentially\n\n - Use AI to extend design capacity and speed without sacrificing quality\n\nCross-Functional Leadership\n\n - Partner closely with Product and Engineering leaders to define strategy and deliver impactful outcomes.\n\n - Collaborate with Brand, Creative and Marketing to ensure a cohesive, end-to-end user experience and that we deliver on a shared brand and product vision for Poshmark\n\n - Partner with Engineering to translate design systems into implementation standards, ensuring consistency across feature development.\n\n - Communicate design decisions clearly and influence stakeholders at all levels\n\n - Coordinate with team members who will report into you, and coordinate design work with you, from our India and Korea offices.\n\n \n \n\n\nWHAT WE’RE LOOKING FOR\n\nExperience\n\n - At least 10–15+ years of experience in product or UX design, with a significant portion in leadership roles\n\n - Proven success building, managing, and scaling design teams, including managing managers\n\n - Experience designing for marketplaces, e-commerce, or social platforms\n\n - Hands-on familiarity with marketplace dynamics, either professionally or as an active participant\n\nDesign & Product Expertise\n\n - Strong portfolio demonstrating high-quality, user-centered design at scale\n\n - Deep expertise in mobile-first consumer products and complex, multi-sided systems\n\n - Strong systems thinking and ability to design for both detail and scale\n\n - Experience using AI design tools like Figma Make or Claude Design\n\n - Good familiarity with experimentation, growth design, and data-informed decision-making\n\nLeadership & Influence\n\n - Strategic mindset with the ability to connect design decisions to business outcomes\n\n - Exceptional communication and storytelling skills\n\n - Ability to influence cross-functional partners and senior leadership\n\n - Experience deploying and driving scale of design work and prototyping through use of AI-based design tools\n\nMarketplace Insight & User Empathy\n\n - Deep understanding of marketplace dynamics, including supply/demand balance, trust, and incentives\n\n - Empathy for diverse user segments, from casual participants to power sellers\n\n - Passion for community-driven, social product experiences\n\n \n \n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Experience with live commerce, creator tools, or social engagement features\n\n - Background or experience with two-sided marketplaces, fashion, retail, resale, or lifestyle marketplaces\n\n \n \n\n\nWHY JOIN POSHMARK\n\n - Shape the future of social commerce at scale\n\n - Lead design for a deeply engaged, entrepreneurial community\n\n - Build experiences that directly impact users’ livelihoods and success\n\n - Work alongside a collaborative, mission-driven team\n\n"},{"id":"ececfb81-83b4-46f3-99b0-040a8a43a268","title":"Growth Marketing Manager, Awareness Media","department":"All Departments","team":"Awareness Team","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"US California (Redwood City) - Office","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-17T22:24:43.530+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Redwood City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/ececfb81-83b4-46f3-99b0-040a8a43a268","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/ececfb81-83b4-46f3-99b0-040a8a43a268/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Poshmark</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Poshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection.</strong> Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the Role</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Poshmark is looking for a Growth Marketing Manager, Awareness Media to own our paid video strategy across multiple channels. You will operate with a builder's mindset - testing new opportunities, scaling what works, and managing both direct campaign execution and agency partnerships to accelerate shopper and seller growth.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will own the strategy and execution across our primary video channels: TV, CTV/OTT, and YouTube, with flexibility to explore opportunities like OOH and network partnerships. You will be equally comfortable building a quarterly media plan as you are optimizing live campaigns. Your work will span both sides of our marketplace as needed with a sophisticated mix of in-house execution and agency partnerships. This role will report to the Director of Growth, Awareness.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and execute Poshmark's integrated video media strategy, balancing brand awareness with intent objectives across TV, CTV, and YouTube</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own end-to-end campaign execution: planning, media buying, performance monitoring, and optimization across all video channels</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Execute campaigns directly where appropriate (YouTube, programmatic placements) and manage relationships with media agencies for TV, premium CTV, and strategic partnerships</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate closely with cross-functional partners across brand, creative, data and engineering</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and run structured experiments to evaluate channel viability and emerging opportunities - setting clear success metrics and synthesizing learnings into actionable recommendations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify the highest-leverage levers across your channel portfolio - audience, creative, buying strategy - and build scalable playbooks to drive efficiency and scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage a dynamic budget across channels and time periods, tracking KPIs and translating performance data into clear insights and action plans for stakeholders</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Negotiate rates, added value, and make-goods with networks, platforms, and media partners to maximize efficiency and secure premium inventory</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate cross-functionally with growth, creative, data, and analytics teams to align media strategy with broader business objectives and quarterly priorities</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About You</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5–8 years managing and executing multi-million dollar campaigns across awareness media channels (TV, CTV/OTT, YouTube), ideally at an e-commerce or high-growth brand</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on-keyboard experience setting up and managing video / CTV campaigns in platforms like CM360, DV360, The Trade Desk, etc.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to manage and optimize multiple channels simultaneously, with a track record of impact through multiple measurement lenses: lift studies, incrementality, MMM, etc.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong negotiation skills and experience securing favorable rates and placements from networks, platforms, and media partners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analytical fluency: comfortable working with large datasets, building performance dashboards, and making budget decisions grounded in data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experimentation mindset: you know how to design rigorous tests, read results objectively, and deprioritize ideas that are not working</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort with ambiguity: you thrive in environments where focus shifts between seller and shopper initiatives and can adapt without losing momentum</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal communication skills with the ability to present channel strategy and results to senior stakeholders clearly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong grasp on media and entertainment trends and calendars within our target audience</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT POSHMARK\n\n\nPoshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection. Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.\n\n \n\nAbout the Role\n\nPoshmark is looking for a Growth Marketing Manager, Awareness Media to own our paid video strategy across multiple channels. You will operate with a builder's mindset - testing new opportunities, scaling what works, and managing both direct campaign execution and agency partnerships to accelerate shopper and seller growth.\n\n \n\nKey Responsibilities\n\nYou will own the strategy and execution across our primary video channels: TV, CTV/OTT, and YouTube, with flexibility to explore opportunities like OOH and network partnerships. You will be equally comfortable building a quarterly media plan as you are optimizing live campaigns. Your work will span both sides of our marketplace as needed with a sophisticated mix of in-house execution and agency partnerships. This role will report to the Director of Growth, Awareness.\n\n - Develop and execute Poshmark's integrated video media strategy, balancing brand awareness with intent objectives across TV, CTV, and YouTube\n\n - Own end-to-end campaign execution: planning, media buying, performance monitoring, and optimization across all video channels\n\n - Execute campaigns directly where appropriate (YouTube, programmatic placements) and manage relationships with media agencies for TV, premium CTV, and strategic partnerships\n\n - Collaborate closely with cross-functional partners across brand, creative, data and engineering\n\n - Design and run structured experiments to evaluate channel viability and emerging opportunities - setting clear success metrics and synthesizing learnings into actionable recommendations\n\n - Identify the highest-leverage levers across your channel portfolio - audience, creative, buying strategy - and build scalable playbooks to drive efficiency and scale\n\n - Manage a dynamic budget across channels and time periods, tracking KPIs and translating performance data into clear insights and action plans for stakeholders\n\n - Negotiate rates, added value, and make-goods with networks, platforms, and media partners to maximize efficiency and secure premium inventory\n\n - Collaborate cross-functionally with growth, creative, data, and analytics teams to align media strategy with broader business objectives and quarterly priorities\n\n\n\nAbout You\n\n - 5–8 years managing and executing multi-million dollar campaigns across awareness media channels (TV, CTV/OTT, YouTube), ideally at an e-commerce or high-growth brand\n\n - Hands-on-keyboard experience setting up and managing video / CTV campaigns in platforms like CM360, DV360, The Trade Desk, etc.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to manage and optimize multiple channels simultaneously, with a track record of impact through multiple measurement lenses: lift studies, incrementality, MMM, etc.\n\n - Strong negotiation skills and experience securing favorable rates and placements from networks, platforms, and media partners\n\n - Analytical fluency: comfortable working with large datasets, building performance dashboards, and making budget decisions grounded in data\n\n - Experimentation mindset: you know how to design rigorous tests, read results objectively, and deprioritize ideas that are not working\n\n - Comfort with ambiguity: you thrive in environments where focus shifts between seller and shopper initiatives and can adapt without losing momentum\n\n - Excellent written and verbal communication skills with the ability to present channel strategy and results to senior stakeholders clearly\n\n - Strong grasp on media and entertainment trends and calendars within our target audience"},{"id":"9815fea8-ac8d-499f-baa0-7a9e7a7bea4d","title":"Director, Posh Live","department":"All Departments","team":"Shows Team","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"US California (Redwood City) - Office","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-03T20:44:32.325+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Redwood City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/9815fea8-ac8d-499f-baa0-7a9e7a7bea4d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/9815fea8-ac8d-499f-baa0-7a9e7a7bea4d/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Poshmark</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Poshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection.</strong> Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong><u>About the Role</u></strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As the business owner for Posh Live, you will own its operating plan, marketplace health, growth strategy, and execution. You will make day-to-day business decisions across supply, demand, product priorities, programming, and marketplace quality while leading a cross-functional organization spanning Product, Engineering, Marketing, Data, and Operations.<br /><br />Success in this role is measured by one thing: whether Posh Live grows into a healthy, scalable business.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a business-owner role reporting to the Head of Posh Live, with real decision-making authority over how the strategy gets built out in practice - including direct management of the Host Acquisition team. You will lead a broader cross-functional group spanning Product, Engineering, Marketing, and Data, set the operating plan and cadence, and be the person accountable when targets are hit or missed. This role is for someone who wants ownership of a growing business line, not just a set of deliverables.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong><u>Responsibilities</u></strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Business Ownership and Accountability</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the detailed operating plan for Posh Live and be directly accountable for the business metrics that matter - growth, engagement, and marketplace health.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Make the day-to-day calls needed to hit targets, escalating only the trade-offs that materially change the strategic direction.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own forecasting and reporting for Posh Live's performance, and make the case for resourcing and investment where needed.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Buyer Experience and Content Strategy</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define what a great buyer experience looks like across Posh Live - discovery, watching, and purchasing - and translate that into clear content and programming standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own curation criteria and programming decisions for premium/flagship content, and be accountable for how well it reflects that buyer experience bar.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Merchandising and key partners on exclusive inventory and content planning.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Host Acquisition and Marketplace Quality</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the strategy and execution playbook for host acquisition, and directly manage the Host Acquisition team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the programs, incentives, and quality mechanisms that grow and maintain a healthy base of hosts/sellers, and be accountable for the resulting supply and quality metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the trade-off between growth in volume and the quality standards that keep the marketplace trustworthy for buyers.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cross-Product Growth and Discovery</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own how Posh Live connects with and reinforces the broader Poshmark experience (search, catalogue, feed), and be accountable for the resulting engagement metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with Product and Engineering to prioritize the features that most strengthen these connections, making the final call on trade-offs within your remit.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cross-Functional Leadership</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead a cross-functional working group spanning Product, Engineering, Marketing, and Data - setting goals, holding partners accountable, and unblocking execution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Own the operating cadence for Posh Live — goal-setting, business reviews, and prioritization frameworks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">•     Define clear roles, responsibilities, and decision rights across partner teams, and be the final decision-maker on the majority of day-to-day trade-offs.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong><u>6-Month Accomplishments</u></strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Took ownership of the business</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stood up a concrete, sequenced operating plan with clear owners, milestones, and metrics - and is running the business against it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Established the operating cadence and reporting rhythm with the Head of Posh Live and cross-functional partners.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Defined and began raising the buyer experience bar</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Defined a clear point of view on what a great buyer experience looks like on Posh Live, and translated it into concrete content and programming standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ran a first cohort of flagship content against these standards.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Defined the host acquisition strategy and got the team executing against it</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Took on management of the Host Acquisition team, defined a clear execution strategy and playbook, and provided hands-on guidance to run against it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Delivered an early, measurable improvement in sourcing, onboarding, or activation performance tied to the new strategy.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Instrumented and began owning cross-product engagement</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Defined and began tracking the core cross-product engagement and discovery metrics as owned KPIs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identified and prioritized 1-2 high-leverage product changes to strengthen these connections.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong><u>12+ Month Accomplishments</u></strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Scaled host acquisition through a proven strategy</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grew host/seller volume through the team's execution of your acquisition strategy and playbook, without degrading quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Can point to specific strategic and management decisions that drove the result.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Established a differentiated buyer experience</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Made Posh Live's buyer experience - anchored by flagship content - a recognizable, differentiated draw that sets the standard for the rest of the marketplace.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proved out cross-product growth loops at scale</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Showed measurable, sustained traffic and engagement flowing between Posh Live and the rest of the Poshmark experience, with clear accountability for the result.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Built a scalable operating engine and earned expanded ownership</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Established a repeatable planning and execution cadence that the team can run without heavy day-to-day involvement from the Head of Posh Live.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Regularly informed strategic refinements with clear, data-backed recommendations, and expanded scope of ownership as trust was established.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong><u>Requirements</u></strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6-10+ years of experience in strategy, business/general management, or product/growth roles, with a track record of owning outcomes - not just delivering plans or analyses.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience managing a team (e.g., acquisition, sales, or partnerships) with clear performance targets is strongly preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in marketplace, e-commerce, social/live commerce, or content/creator platforms strongly preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to take a strategic direction set by others and run a business against it, making independent calls within a clear mandate.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort owning pricing/fee structures, marketplace supply/demand levers, and quality-vs-volume trade-offs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong quantitative and analytical skills; comfortable owning KPIs, building forecasts, and being held accountable for hitting them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to lead cross-functionally and drive accountability without direct reporting authority.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills; comfortable making the case for resourcing and flagging real trade-offs to senior leadership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High ownership and bias to action; comfortable running a business day to day in a fast-moving, still-emerging environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience with live shopping, video commerce, or creator economy businesses is a strong plus.</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT POSHMARK\n\n\nPoshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection. Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.\n\n \n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAs the business owner for Posh Live, you will own its operating plan, marketplace health, growth strategy, and execution. You will make day-to-day business decisions across supply, demand, product priorities, programming, and marketplace quality while leading a cross-functional organization spanning Product, Engineering, Marketing, Data, and Operations.\n\nSuccess in this role is measured by one thing: whether Posh Live grows into a healthy, scalable business.\n\nThis is a business-owner role reporting to the Head of Posh Live, with real decision-making authority over how the strategy gets built out in practice - including direct management of the Host Acquisition team. You will lead a broader cross-functional group spanning Product, Engineering, Marketing, and Data, set the operating plan and cadence, and be the person accountable when targets are hit or missed. This role is for someone who wants ownership of a growing business line, not just a set of deliverables.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\nBusiness Ownership and Accountability\n\n - Own the detailed operating plan for Posh Live and be directly accountable for the business metrics that matter - growth, engagement, and marketplace health.\n\n - Make the day-to-day calls needed to hit targets, escalating only the trade-offs that materially change the strategic direction.\n\n - Own forecasting and reporting for Posh Live's performance, and make the case for resourcing and investment where needed.\n\nBuyer Experience and Content Strategy\n\n - Define what a great buyer experience looks like across Posh Live - discovery, watching, and purchasing - and translate that into clear content and programming standards.\n\n - Own curation criteria and programming decisions for premium/flagship content, and be accountable for how well it reflects that buyer experience bar.\n\n - Partner with Merchandising and key partners on exclusive inventory and content planning.\n\nHost Acquisition and Marketplace Quality\n\n - Own the strategy and execution playbook for host acquisition, and directly manage the Host Acquisition team\n\n - Own the programs, incentives, and quality mechanisms that grow and maintain a healthy base of hosts/sellers, and be accountable for the resulting supply and quality metrics.\n\n - Own the trade-off between growth in volume and the quality standards that keep the marketplace trustworthy for buyers.\n\nCross-Product Growth and Discovery\n\n - Own how Posh Live connects with and reinforces the broader Poshmark experience (search, catalogue, feed), and be accountable for the resulting engagement metrics.\n\n - Work with Product and Engineering to prioritize the features that most strengthen these connections, making the final call on trade-offs within your remit.\n\nCross-Functional Leadership\n\n - Lead a cross-functional working group spanning Product, Engineering, Marketing, and Data - setting goals, holding partners accountable, and unblocking execution.\n\n - •     Own the operating cadence for Posh Live — goal-setting, business reviews, and prioritization frameworks.\n\n - •     Define clear roles, responsibilities, and decision rights across partner teams, and be the final decision-maker on the majority of day-to-day trade-offs.\n\n\n\n\n6-MONTH ACCOMPLISHMENTS\n\nTook ownership of the business\n\n - Stood up a concrete, sequenced operating plan with clear owners, milestones, and metrics - and is running the business against it.\n\n - Established the operating cadence and reporting rhythm with the Head of Posh Live and cross-functional partners.\n\nDefined and began raising the buyer experience bar\n\n - Defined a clear point of view on what a great buyer experience looks like on Posh Live, and translated it into concrete content and programming standards.\n\n - Ran a first cohort of flagship content against these standards.\n\nDefined the host acquisition strategy and got the team executing against it\n\n - Took on management of the Host Acquisition team, defined a clear execution strategy and playbook, and provided hands-on guidance to run against it.\n\n - Delivered an early, measurable improvement in sourcing, onboarding, or activation performance tied to the new strategy.\n\nInstrumented and began owning cross-product engagement\n\n - Defined and began tracking the core cross-product engagement and discovery metrics as owned KPIs.\n\n - Identified and prioritized 1-2 high-leverage product changes to strengthen these connections.\n\n\n\n\n12+ MONTH ACCOMPLISHMENTS\n\nScaled host acquisition through a proven strategy\n\n - Grew host/seller volume through the team's execution of your acquisition strategy and playbook, without degrading quality.\n\n - Can point to specific strategic and management decisions that drove the result.\n\nEstablished a differentiated buyer experience\n\n - Made Posh Live's buyer experience - anchored by flagship content - a recognizable, differentiated draw that sets the standard for the rest of the marketplace.\n\nProved out cross-product growth loops at scale\n\n - Showed measurable, sustained traffic and engagement flowing between Posh Live and the rest of the Poshmark experience, with clear accountability for the result.\n\nBuilt a scalable operating engine and earned expanded ownership\n\n - Established a repeatable planning and execution cadence that the team can run without heavy day-to-day involvement from the Head of Posh Live.\n\n - Regularly informed strategic refinements with clear, data-backed recommendations, and expanded scope of ownership as trust was established.\n\n\n\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n\n - 6-10+ years of experience in strategy, business/general management, or product/growth roles, with a track record of owning outcomes - not just delivering plans or analyses.\n\n - Prior experience managing a team (e.g., acquisition, sales, or partnerships) with clear performance targets is strongly preferred.\n\n - Experience in marketplace, e-commerce, social/live commerce, or content/creator platforms strongly preferred.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to take a strategic direction set by others and run a business against it, making independent calls within a clear mandate.\n\n - Comfort owning pricing/fee structures, marketplace supply/demand levers, and quality-vs-volume trade-offs.\n\n - Strong quantitative and analytical skills; comfortable owning KPIs, building forecasts, and being held accountable for hitting them.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to lead cross-functionally and drive accountability without direct reporting authority.\n\n - Excellent communication skills; comfortable making the case for resourcing and flagging real trade-offs to senior leadership.\n\n - High ownership and bias to action; comfortable running a business day to day in a fast-moving, still-emerging environment.\n\n - Prior experience with live shopping, video commerce, or creator economy businesses is a strong plus."},{"id":"e0557a25-dde6-4b98-88cd-bc185f703452","title":"Sr. Manager, Product Marketing (Posh Live)","department":"All Departments","team":"Product Marketing Team","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"US California (Redwood City) - Office","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-13T01:36:12.759+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Redwood City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/e0557a25-dde6-4b98-88cd-bc185f703452","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/e0557a25-dde6-4b98-88cd-bc185f703452/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Poshmark</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Poshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection.</strong> Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Sr. Manager, Product Marketing (Posh Live) sits at the intersection of Product, Growth, Community, and Content, working closely with the Director of Product Marketing and the GM of Posh Live. This role defines how Posh Live shows up to buyers and sellers - shaping positioning, messaging, and go-to-market strategies that drive adoption, engagement, and growth for Poshmark's live shopping product.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Critically, this role starts from the buyer. You will build a deep, first-hand understanding of why and how buyers discover, watch, and purchase through live shows, and use that understanding to define what it takes for a brand or enterprise seller to actually succeed on Show. Seller-facing value propositions, enablement content, and playbooks should all be grounded in real buyer behavior and demand - not written from the seller side in. This role is both strategic and highly hands-on, with day-to-day cross-functional execution.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Buyer Insight as the Foundation for Seller Success</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build a deep, data-informed understanding of buyer behavior on Show: discovery and viewing patterns, what drives watch time and purchase, category and price sensitivity, and trust/loyalty drivers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Translate buyer insight into a clear point of view on what makes a show, host, or category successful - and use that to define what \"good\" looks like for brand and enterprise sellers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Continuously feed buyer-side learnings back into seller-facing strategy, content, and product requirements.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Brand and Enterprise Seller Value Proposition and Playbooks</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define the value proposition for brand and enterprise sellers hosting on Show, anchored in demonstrated buyer demand rather than assumptions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and maintain playbooks that help brand and enterprise hosts plan, run, and optimize shows - grounded in what actually drives buyer engagement and conversion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Supply/Partnerships and Merchandising to ensure onboarding, enablement, and success materials for brand/enterprise sellers reflect current buyer insight.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define success metrics for brand/enterprise sellers on Show and identify the levers that most reliably improve them.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish comprehensive seller educational programs and trust guidelines that teach enterprise brands how to maintain compliance, protect their reputation, and build long-term buyer loyalty during live broadcasts.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Product Narrative, Positioning, and Messaging</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define value propositions and messaging frameworks for buyers and sellers across the Show experience — discovery, live interactions, hosting tools, and checkout.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop clear, compelling narratives that translate the mechanics of live shopping into simple, user-centric benefits for both sides of the marketplace.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure consistent storytelling across in-product, lifecycle, marketing, and external channels.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>GTM Strategy for Launches and Enhancements</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead GTM strategy for new Show features and enhancements, including:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Feature positioning and differentiation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Target segmentation across buyer segments and host tiers (including brand/enterprise)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Rollout plans, pilots, and experimentation frameworks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Launch KPIs, adoption goals, and success measurement</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Product, Growth, and Analytics to execute launches with impact.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>6-Month Accomplishments</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Built a rigorous, buyer-first understanding of Show</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Synthesized qualitative and quantitative insight into why and how buyers discover, watch, and purchase on Show.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identified 2-3 high-leverage buyer insights that directly inform seller strategy, messaging, or the product roadmap.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Defined the brand/enterprise seller value proposition and first playbook</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Published a clear, buyer-grounded value proposition for brand and enterprise sellers hosting on Show.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Shipped a first version of a seller playbook, built from buyer/engagement data rather than seller assumptions.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Established a clear, unified Show product narrative</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Developed and socialized a core messaging and positioning framework for buyers and sellers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Aligned cross-functional partners on who Show is for, what problem it solves, and why it matters.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Built a strong cross-functional operating cadence</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Established trusted working relationships with Product, Growth, Data Analytics, Supply/Partnerships, and the GM's team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Defined clear GTM roles, responsibilities, and decision rights for major launches.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>12+ Month Accomplishments</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Made brand/enterprise seller success a repeatable, buyer-grounded motion</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evolved playbooks and enablement materials into a durable system that scales with new brand/enterprise sellers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated clear improvement in brand/enterprise seller outcomes (e.g., show performance, conversion, repeat hosting) tied to buyer insight-driven changes.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Institutionalized product marketing excellence for Show</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Embedded consistent positioning and storytelling across in-product, lifecycle, and external channels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Created durable frameworks and tooling that enable the team to scale launches and messaging efficiently.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Driven measurable adoption and engagement outcomes</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated clear impact on buyer watch time, conversion, repeat viewership, and show volume.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improved launch performance through experimentation, segmentation, and iteration.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Influenced Show strategy through user and market insight</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Regularly surfaced actionable insights that shape Show's roadmap and go-to-market decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Helped identify new growth opportunities across categories, buyer segments, or seller tiers.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Requirements</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5-8 years of experience in product marketing, growth marketing, or lifecycle marketing, ideally at a marketplace, social commerce, or live/video commerce company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to build deep consumer/buyer insight and translate it into seller- or partner-facing strategy and enablement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building playbooks or enablement materials for B2B2C partners, brands, or enterprise accounts is a strong plus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of driving adoption and engagement for a product in an early or scaling phase.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong ability to translate complex product mechanics into clear, user-centric value propositions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort working with data and analytics to define success, measure impact, and inform decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong collaborator with experience influencing without authority across Product, Growth, Supply/Partnerships, and Analytics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal storytelling skills, comfortable writing for both consumer and brand/enterprise audiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bias toward action, testing, and iteration; comfort operating in ambiguity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Genuine interest in resale, social commerce, and/or live shopping formats is a strong plus.</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT POSHMARK\n\n\nPoshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection. Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.\n\n \n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nThe Sr. Manager, Product Marketing (Posh Live) sits at the intersection of Product, Growth, Community, and Content, working closely with the Director of Product Marketing and the GM of Posh Live. This role defines how Posh Live shows up to buyers and sellers - shaping positioning, messaging, and go-to-market strategies that drive adoption, engagement, and growth for Poshmark's live shopping product.\n\nCritically, this role starts from the buyer. You will build a deep, first-hand understanding of why and how buyers discover, watch, and purchase through live shows, and use that understanding to define what it takes for a brand or enterprise seller to actually succeed on Show. Seller-facing value propositions, enablement content, and playbooks should all be grounded in real buyer behavior and demand - not written from the seller side in. This role is both strategic and highly hands-on, with day-to-day cross-functional execution.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\nBuyer Insight as the Foundation for Seller Success\n\n - Build a deep, data-informed understanding of buyer behavior on Show: discovery and viewing patterns, what drives watch time and purchase, category and price sensitivity, and trust/loyalty drivers.\n\n - Translate buyer insight into a clear point of view on what makes a show, host, or category successful - and use that to define what \"good\" looks like for brand and enterprise sellers.\n\n - Continuously feed buyer-side learnings back into seller-facing strategy, content, and product requirements.\n\nBrand and Enterprise Seller Value Proposition and Playbooks\n\n - Define the value proposition for brand and enterprise sellers hosting on Show, anchored in demonstrated buyer demand rather than assumptions.\n\n - Build and maintain playbooks that help brand and enterprise hosts plan, run, and optimize shows - grounded in what actually drives buyer engagement and conversion.\n\n - Partner with Supply/Partnerships and Merchandising to ensure onboarding, enablement, and success materials for brand/enterprise sellers reflect current buyer insight.\n\n - Define success metrics for brand/enterprise sellers on Show and identify the levers that most reliably improve them.\n\n - Establish comprehensive seller educational programs and trust guidelines that teach enterprise brands how to maintain compliance, protect their reputation, and build long-term buyer loyalty during live broadcasts.\n\nProduct Narrative, Positioning, and Messaging\n\n - Define value propositions and messaging frameworks for buyers and sellers across the Show experience — discovery, live interactions, hosting tools, and checkout.\n\n - Develop clear, compelling narratives that translate the mechanics of live shopping into simple, user-centric benefits for both sides of the marketplace.\n\n - Ensure consistent storytelling across in-product, lifecycle, marketing, and external channels.\n\nGTM Strategy for Launches and Enhancements\n\n - Lead GTM strategy for new Show features and enhancements, including:\n   \n   - Feature positioning and differentiation\n   \n   - Target segmentation across buyer segments and host tiers (including brand/enterprise)\n   \n   - Rollout plans, pilots, and experimentation frameworks\n   \n   - Launch KPIs, adoption goals, and success measurement\n\n - Partner closely with Product, Growth, and Analytics to execute launches with impact.\n\n\n6-MONTH ACCOMPLISHMENTS\n\nBuilt a rigorous, buyer-first understanding of Show\n\n - Synthesized qualitative and quantitative insight into why and how buyers discover, watch, and purchase on Show.\n\n - Identified 2-3 high-leverage buyer insights that directly inform seller strategy, messaging, or the product roadmap.\n\nDefined the brand/enterprise seller value proposition and first playbook\n\n - Published a clear, buyer-grounded value proposition for brand and enterprise sellers hosting on Show.\n\n - Shipped a first version of a seller playbook, built from buyer/engagement data rather than seller assumptions.\n\nEstablished a clear, unified Show product narrative\n\n - Developed and socialized a core messaging and positioning framework for buyers and sellers.\n\n - Aligned cross-functional partners on who Show is for, what problem it solves, and why it matters.\n\nBuilt a strong cross-functional operating cadence\n\n - Established trusted working relationships with Product, Growth, Data Analytics, Supply/Partnerships, and the GM's team.\n\n - Defined clear GTM roles, responsibilities, and decision rights for major launches.\n\n\n12+ MONTH ACCOMPLISHMENTS\n\nMade brand/enterprise seller success a repeatable, buyer-grounded motion\n\n - Evolved playbooks and enablement materials into a durable system that scales with new brand/enterprise sellers.\n\n - Demonstrated clear improvement in brand/enterprise seller outcomes (e.g., show performance, conversion, repeat hosting) tied to buyer insight-driven changes.\n\nInstitutionalized product marketing excellence for Show\n\n - Embedded consistent positioning and storytelling across in-product, lifecycle, and external channels.\n\n - Created durable frameworks and tooling that enable the team to scale launches and messaging efficiently.\n\nDriven measurable adoption and engagement outcomes\n\n - Demonstrated clear impact on buyer watch time, conversion, repeat viewership, and show volume.\n\n - Improved launch performance through experimentation, segmentation, and iteration.\n\nInfluenced Show strategy through user and market insight\n\n - Regularly surfaced actionable insights that shape Show's roadmap and go-to-market decisions.\n\n - Helped identify new growth opportunities across categories, buyer segments, or seller tiers.\n\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n\n - 5-8 years of experience in product marketing, growth marketing, or lifecycle marketing, ideally at a marketplace, social commerce, or live/video commerce company.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to build deep consumer/buyer insight and translate it into seller- or partner-facing strategy and enablement.\n\n - Experience building playbooks or enablement materials for B2B2C partners, brands, or enterprise accounts is a strong plus.\n\n - Track record of driving adoption and engagement for a product in an early or scaling phase.\n\n - Strong ability to translate complex product mechanics into clear, user-centric value propositions.\n\n - Comfort working with data and analytics to define success, measure impact, and inform decisions.\n\n - Strong collaborator with experience influencing without authority across Product, Growth, Supply/Partnerships, and Analytics.\n\n - Excellent written and verbal storytelling skills, comfortable writing for both consumer and brand/enterprise audiences.\n\n - Bias toward action, testing, and iteration; comfort operating in ambiguity.\n\n - Genuine interest in resale, social commerce, and/or live shopping formats is a strong plus."},{"id":"8a05e792-ee3f-45a6-ae3b-591809faf18a","title":"Director, Financial Crimes Compliance - AML Officer","department":"All Departments","team":"Payments & Compliance","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"US California (Redwood City) - Office","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-24T19:40:06.483+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Redwood City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/8a05e792-ee3f-45a6-ae3b-591809faf18a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/8a05e792-ee3f-45a6-ae3b-591809faf18a/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Poshmark</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Poshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection.</strong> Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Director, Financial Crimes Compliance – AML Officer is the designated US governance owner for Poshmark’s Financial Crimes Compliance program. This role owns the BSA/AML program, the compliance policy and risk framework, and the governance structure required to make the program audit-ready, banking-partner-ready, and scalable.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Director is accountable for regulatory interpretation, program-level risk assessment, sanctions governance, escalation standards, training substance, audit response, and active oversight of Financial Crimes Operations. This role also owns executive reporting and program health monitoring, and serves as the primary compliance point of contact for internal leadership, external auditors, and banking partners.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Director partners closely with Risk Strategy on seller identity and related risk controls. Risk Strategy owns vendor selection and vendor performance management for the underlying identity / risk tooling stack, while Financial Crimes Compliance defines the regulatory requirements, control standards, and acceptance criteria that the program must satisfy.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2>Core Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Program Ownership:</strong> Own and maintain Poshmark’s BSA/AML program, including annual risk assessment, governance cadence, and program documentation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Policy Governance:</strong> Own compliance policy governance for seller identity, KYC/KYB, sanctions screening, and high-risk seller review control standards.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Risk Strategy Partnership:</strong> Partner with Risk Strategy on the seller identity / KYC / KYB / sanctions program by defining regulatory requirements, control standards, acceptance criteria, and escalation rules for the program.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>External Liaison:</strong> Serve as the primary US governance point of contact for banking partners, external auditors, and regulators.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Executive &amp; Health Reporting:</strong> Own executive reporting and program health reporting, including BSA/AML trends, sanctions screening performance, escalation volumes, control effectiveness, and operational quality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Training Oversight:</strong> Own the compliance curriculum and sign off on training before Financial Crimes Operations delivers it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Cross-Functional Roadmap:</strong> Drive the Financial Crimes Compliance program roadmap with Product, Engineering, and Operations, including business requirements, control design, user-facing workflow design, terms/policy implications, and support content requirements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Pre-Go-Live Sign-Off:</strong> Review and approve controls before go-live, including the compliance requirements for new workflows, tooling, and product changes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Vendor Governance:</strong> Own the full lifecycle of Financial Crimes Compliance vendor partnerships from a compliance perspective, including business requirements, implementation oversight, ongoing business reviews, and partnership with Product, Legal, and Contracts as needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Detection &amp; System Monitoring:</strong> Provide detection logic oversight and ongoing program health monitoring, including decision logic calibration, feedback-loop analysis, control performance review, and oversight of the admin functionality and access controls required to operate the program safely and consistently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>SAR Filing Governance:</strong> Own SAR filing governance and reporting operations in partnership with the AML Escalation Manager, including escalation standards, filing decision oversight, documentation quality, and audit-ready recordkeeping.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Audit Leadership:</strong> Lead audit preparation and response, including evidence organization, control narratives, and remediation tracking.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Operational Oversight &amp; Intervention:</strong> Maintain active knowledge of Financial Crimes Compliance Operations execution quality, identify gaps between policy intent and operational reality, and intervene when execution creates compliance risk.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Procedure Approval:</strong> Review and approve Financial Crimes Compliance Operations operational procedures before implementation.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2>Qualifications</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience:</strong> 7+ years of experience in BSA/AML, sanctions, financial crimes compliance, or a closely related discipline.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Certifications:</strong> CAMS / ACAMS or equivalent certification required.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Regulatory Knowledge:</strong> Strong working knowledge of BSA, AML, OFAC, the USA PATRIOT Act, FinCEN expectations, and AMLA 2020.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Exam &amp; Audit Management:</strong> Direct experience managing regulatory exams, banking partner relationships, and audit-ready compliance programs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical &amp; Workflow Integration:</strong> Experience translating regulatory requirements into business requirements, workflows, support content, and operational controls.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Vendor &amp; Cross-Functional Leadership:</strong> Experience with vendor management, cross-functional program leadership, and senior stakeholder management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Communication &amp; Influence:</strong> Strong executive communication skills and the ability to influence across Product, Engineering, Operations, Legal, and Finance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Education:</strong> Bachelor’s degree preferred; advanced degree a plus.</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT POSHMARK\n\n\nPoshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection. Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.\n\n \n\nThe Director, Financial Crimes Compliance – AML Officer is the designated US governance owner for Poshmark’s Financial Crimes Compliance program. This role owns the BSA/AML program, the compliance policy and risk framework, and the governance structure required to make the program audit-ready, banking-partner-ready, and scalable.\n\n \n\nThe Director is accountable for regulatory interpretation, program-level risk assessment, sanctions governance, escalation standards, training substance, audit response, and active oversight of Financial Crimes Operations. This role also owns executive reporting and program health monitoring, and serves as the primary compliance point of contact for internal leadership, external auditors, and banking partners.\n\n \n\nThe Director partners closely with Risk Strategy on seller identity and related risk controls. Risk Strategy owns vendor selection and vendor performance management for the underlying identity / risk tooling stack, while Financial Crimes Compliance defines the regulatory requirements, control standards, and acceptance criteria that the program must satisfy.\n\n \n\n\nCORE RESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Program Ownership: Own and maintain Poshmark’s BSA/AML program, including annual risk assessment, governance cadence, and program documentation.\n\n - Policy Governance: Own compliance policy governance for seller identity, KYC/KYB, sanctions screening, and high-risk seller review control standards.\n\n - Risk Strategy Partnership: Partner with Risk Strategy on the seller identity / KYC / KYB / sanctions program by defining regulatory requirements, control standards, acceptance criteria, and escalation rules for the program.\n\n - External Liaison: Serve as the primary US governance point of contact for banking partners, external auditors, and regulators.\n\n - Executive & Health Reporting: Own executive reporting and program health reporting, including BSA/AML trends, sanctions screening performance, escalation volumes, control effectiveness, and operational quality.\n\n - Training Oversight: Own the compliance curriculum and sign off on training before Financial Crimes Operations delivers it.\n\n - Cross-Functional Roadmap: Drive the Financial Crimes Compliance program roadmap with Product, Engineering, and Operations, including business requirements, control design, user-facing workflow design, terms/policy implications, and support content requirements.\n\n - Pre-Go-Live Sign-Off: Review and approve controls before go-live, including the compliance requirements for new workflows, tooling, and product changes.\n\n - Vendor Governance: Own the full lifecycle of Financial Crimes Compliance vendor partnerships from a compliance perspective, including business requirements, implementation oversight, ongoing business reviews, and partnership with Product, Legal, and Contracts as needed.\n\n - Detection & System Monitoring: Provide detection logic oversight and ongoing program health monitoring, including decision logic calibration, feedback-loop analysis, control performance review, and oversight of the admin functionality and access controls required to operate the program safely and consistently.\n\n - SAR Filing Governance: Own SAR filing governance and reporting operations in partnership with the AML Escalation Manager, including escalation standards, filing decision oversight, documentation quality, and audit-ready recordkeeping.\n\n - Audit Leadership: Lead audit preparation and response, including evidence organization, control narratives, and remediation tracking.\n\n - Operational Oversight & Intervention: Maintain active knowledge of Financial Crimes Compliance Operations execution quality, identify gaps between policy intent and operational reality, and intervene when execution creates compliance risk.\n\n - Procedure Approval: Review and approve Financial Crimes Compliance Operations operational procedures before implementation.\n\n \n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\n - Experience: 7+ years of experience in BSA/AML, sanctions, financial crimes compliance, or a closely related discipline.\n\n - Certifications: CAMS / ACAMS or equivalent certification required.\n\n - Regulatory Knowledge: Strong working knowledge of BSA, AML, OFAC, the USA PATRIOT Act, FinCEN expectations, and AMLA 2020.\n\n - Exam & Audit Management: Direct experience managing regulatory exams, banking partner relationships, and audit-ready compliance programs.\n\n - Technical & Workflow Integration: Experience translating regulatory requirements into business requirements, workflows, support content, and operational controls.\n\n - Vendor & Cross-Functional Leadership: Experience with vendor management, cross-functional program leadership, and senior stakeholder management.\n\n - Communication & Influence: Strong executive communication skills and the ability to influence across Product, Engineering, Operations, Legal, and Finance.\n\n - Education: Bachelor’s degree preferred; advanced degree a plus."},{"id":"5ed99cb0-d860-4c96-aa93-31c82af1ade7","title":"Live Chat Support Associate (1-3 years)","department":"All Departments","team":"Scaled Support Team","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"IN Tamil Nadu (Chennai) - Office","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-26T09:30:29.412+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"India","addressLocality":"Chennai"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/5ed99cb0-d860-4c96-aa93-31c82af1ade7","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/5ed99cb0-d860-4c96-aa93-31c82af1ade7/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Poshmark</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Poshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection.</strong> Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Poshmark is the largest community marketplace for fashion, where anyone can buy, sell, and share their personal style. As a Community Associate, you provide front-line support to our growing community — today primarily over email, messenger, and social channels, and increasingly through live chat as we roll out this new real-time channel.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll triage and resolve time-sensitive inquiries about orders, accounts, shipping, and payments, and provide product education, all while maintaining a high bar for customer satisfaction. As live chat rolls out, you'll also take on real-time conversations: understanding intent and writing clearly under time pressure, making routing and escalation calls in the moment, and building up to handling multiple chats at once as you gain experience. The ideal Community Associate...</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understands user issues with empathy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exercises strong problem-solving skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Is patient in understanding and responding to our users</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Is comfortable switching between async (email) and real-time (chat) modes of support as needed</p></li></ul><h2>What You'll Do</h2><h2>Email &amp; General Support</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engage with Poshmark users via email, messenger, and/or social support</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond to users in a timely, friendly, and professional manner</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrate empathy through thoughtful and prompt resolutions for the community</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research, troubleshoot, and recommend solutions for open orders and account-related issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gather feedback and suggestions from the community</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strive to exceed volume and CSAT (customer satisfaction) goals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help with other projects and administrative work as needed</p></li></ul><h2>Live Chat (as rolled out)</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond to live chat conversations promptly and accurately - helping users with orders, shipping, payments, listings, and account questions in real time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understand user intent and write clearly and concisely under time pressure; set expectations during research or hold time (e.g., “Give me one moment while I look into this”) so the customer is never left wondering what's happening</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Apply the escalation framework to each conversation: i) resolve directly, ii) warm-hand-off to a specialized team or iii) log an offline case — capturing the right details and keeping the customer informed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">De-escalate frustrated customers using active listening and ownership language, adapting your approach mid-conversation as needed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Navigate the chat platform, knowledge base, order/CRM history, and internal case tools quickly enough to find answers live, without stalling the conversation<br />Progress through a structured concurrency ramp: one chat during training, two after graduation, and up to three in normal production (more during peak sales/seasonal events), advancing only once quality and speed are consistently on target</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use approved macros and response templates as a starting point, not a script — personalize responses so the conversation still feels human</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><h1>Growth &amp; Accomplishments</h1><h2>3-6-Month Accomplishments</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Independently handle email cases with efficiency and accuracy, per guidelines and policy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meet daily case goals on a consistent basis</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Complete live chat training and certification; graduate to handling one / two concurrent chats</p></li></ul><h2>6-12 Month Accomplishments</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Navigate cases with ease across email and chat</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Handle up to three concurrent chats (more during peak events) while holding quality steady</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Begin providing mentorship and guidance to new team members and peers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Begin contributing to team projects and process improvements</p></li></ul><h1>Requirements</h1><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's degree in any discipline.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enthusiastic about community and customer service, with endless patience and a positive attitude.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">1–3 years of total experience, including 6–12 months in customer service; prior live chat experience is a plus (training and a graduation period are provided)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional written communication skills: clear, grammatically clean, and warm in tone, even when writing quickly or under time pressure</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong computer and typing skills; typing speed of at least 40 WPM at 95%+ accuracy (50+ WPM preferred once handling concurrent chats)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Sound judgment for triaging issues — knowing what to resolve yourself, hand off, or log as a case</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Composure under pressure: calm, empathetic, and solution-focused with an upset or unpredictable customer</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable working across multiple tools at once (chat platform, CRM/order system, knowledge base) without losing pace</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Believes that helping users is crucial to the growth and success of the company; values one’s own and team’s success,</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible availability, open to shift rotations, including IST evening/morning hours, and willingness to work on-site during training / live chat rollout phase.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Live chat experience in e-commerce or marketplace platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with Salesforce Service Cloud or a comparable chat/CRM platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Recent experience already handling 2–3+ concurrent chats in a previous role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with dispute resolution, trust &amp; safety, or fraud-related support scenarios</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT POSHMARK\n\n\nPoshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection. Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.\n\n \n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nPoshmark is the largest community marketplace for fashion, where anyone can buy, sell, and share their personal style. As a Community Associate, you provide front-line support to our growing community — today primarily over email, messenger, and social channels, and increasingly through live chat as we roll out this new real-time channel.\n\nYou'll triage and resolve time-sensitive inquiries about orders, accounts, shipping, and payments, and provide product education, all while maintaining a high bar for customer satisfaction. As live chat rolls out, you'll also take on real-time conversations: understanding intent and writing clearly under time pressure, making routing and escalation calls in the moment, and building up to handling multiple chats at once as you gain experience. The ideal Community Associate...\n\n - Understands user issues with empathy\n\n - Exercises strong problem-solving skills\n\n - Is patient in understanding and responding to our users\n\n - Is comfortable switching between async (email) and real-time (chat) modes of support as needed\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n\nEMAIL & GENERAL SUPPORT\n\n - Engage with Poshmark users via email, messenger, and/or social support\n\n - Respond to users in a timely, friendly, and professional manner\n\n - Demonstrate empathy through thoughtful and prompt resolutions for the community\n\n - Research, troubleshoot, and recommend solutions for open orders and account-related issues\n\n - Gather feedback and suggestions from the community\n\n - Strive to exceed volume and CSAT (customer satisfaction) goals\n\n - Help with other projects and administrative work as needed\n\n\nLIVE CHAT (AS ROLLED OUT)\n\n - Respond to live chat conversations promptly and accurately - helping users with orders, shipping, payments, listings, and account questions in real time\n\n - Understand user intent and write clearly and concisely under time pressure; set expectations during research or hold time (e.g., “Give me one moment while I look into this”) so the customer is never left wondering what's happening\n\n - Apply the escalation framework to each conversation: i) resolve directly, ii) warm-hand-off to a specialized team or iii) log an offline case — capturing the right details and keeping the customer informed\n\n - De-escalate frustrated customers using active listening and ownership language, adapting your approach mid-conversation as needed\n\n - Navigate the chat platform, knowledge base, order/CRM history, and internal case tools quickly enough to find answers live, without stalling the conversation\n   Progress through a structured concurrency ramp: one chat during training, two after graduation, and up to three in normal production (more during peak sales/seasonal events), advancing only once quality and speed are consistently on target\n\n - Use approved macros and response templates as a starting point, not a script — personalize responses so the conversation still feels human\n   \n   \n\n\nGROWTH & ACCOMPLISHMENTS\n\n\n3-6-MONTH ACCOMPLISHMENTS\n\n - Independently handle email cases with efficiency and accuracy, per guidelines and policy\n\n - Meet daily case goals on a consistent basis\n\n - Complete live chat training and certification; graduate to handling one / two concurrent chats\n\n\n6-12 MONTH ACCOMPLISHMENTS\n\n - Navigate cases with ease across email and chat\n\n - Handle up to three concurrent chats (more during peak events) while holding quality steady\n\n - Begin providing mentorship and guidance to new team members and peers\n\n - Begin contributing to team projects and process improvements\n\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n\n - Bachelor's degree in any discipline.\n\n - Enthusiastic about community and customer service, with endless patience and a positive attitude.\n\n - 1–3 years of total experience, including 6–12 months in customer service; prior live chat experience is a plus (training and a graduation period are provided)\n\n - Exceptional written communication skills: clear, grammatically clean, and warm in tone, even when writing quickly or under time pressure\n\n - Strong computer and typing skills; typing speed of at least 40 WPM at 95%+ accuracy (50+ WPM preferred once handling concurrent chats)\n\n - Sound judgment for triaging issues — knowing what to resolve yourself, hand off, or log as a case\n\n - Composure under pressure: calm, empathetic, and solution-focused with an upset or unpredictable customer\n\n - Comfortable working across multiple tools at once (chat platform, CRM/order system, knowledge base) without losing pace\n\n - Believes that helping users is crucial to the growth and success of the company; values one’s own and team’s success,\n\n - Flexible availability, open to shift rotations, including IST evening/morning hours, and willingness to work on-site during training / live chat rollout phase.\n\n\nNICE TO HAVE\n\n - Live chat experience in e-commerce or marketplace platforms\n\n - Hands-on experience with Salesforce Service Cloud or a comparable chat/CRM platform\n\n - Recent experience already handling 2–3+ concurrent chats in a previous role\n\n - Experience with dispute resolution, trust & safety, or fraud-related support scenarios"},{"id":"be164aec-878b-493f-8baf-608dc5076b80","title":"Junior Email Support - Night Shift (0 - 3 years only)  ","department":"All Departments","team":"Scaled Support Team","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"IN Tamil Nadu (Chennai) - Office","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-11-04T17:05:20.547+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"India","addressLocality":"Chennai"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/be164aec-878b-493f-8baf-608dc5076b80","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/be164aec-878b-493f-8baf-608dc5076b80/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Poshmark</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Poshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection.</strong> Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Poshmark is the largest community marketplace for fashion where anyone can buy, sell and share their personal style. With millions of shoppers and seller stylists, Poshmark brings together a vibrant community every day to express themselves and share their love of fashion.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a <strong>Community Associate, Disputes </strong>you are responsible for providing front-line customer support to our growing Community.  You will triage and respond to high volumes of time-sensitive customer inquiries--related to orders, their account, and provide detailed product education.  Our goal is to maintain a high level of customer satisfaction while assisting with a seamless user experience. Your ability to investigate, resolve issues, and communicate effectively will be critical in maintaining Poshmark’s high standards of customer satisfaction.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The ideal Community Associate...</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">understands empathy is the key to helping others</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">exercises strong problem-solving skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">showcases endless patience and contagious positive energy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">has excellent written and verbal English communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Is self motivated and thrives working independently.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engage with Poshmark users regarding dispute cases via email support</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Investigate all aspects of an order and find resolutions for dispute cases filed by buyers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond to users in a timely, friendly, and professional manner</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Execute decisions to fairly resolve disputes following Poshmark’s return policies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate with Poshmark users in a friendly, helpful, and patient manner via email</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Gather feedback and suggestions from the Community</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strive to exceed Volume, First Response Time, Resolution Rate and CES (Customer Effort Score) goals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexibility to work on holidays and occasional overtime, as required.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Requirements:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Overnight shift</strong>: 7:30pm/9:30pm/11:30pm  Sun-Thurs/Tues-Sat/Fri-Tues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AUS shift</strong>: 3:30am IST  Sun-Thurs/Tues-Sat/Fri-Tues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">0-3 years of equivalent experience in customer service or community support, particularly in e-commerce. Customer service via email using Salesforce or previous support experience dealing with US-Based customers preferred; new college graduates are encouraged to apply</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong Macbook navigation and typing skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent written and verbal English communication skills, with keen attention to detail</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willing to work on holidays and provide support over weekends, as required</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Problem-solving mindset with the ability to work independently and as part of a team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to collaborate and interact with managers and peers primarily from the US office headquarters with professionalism</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Enthusiastic about community, customer service, and spreading love and kindness</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Endless patience and a positive attitude with the ability to turn a negative into a positive.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive by nature; thrives off the success of a team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Believes that helping users is crucial to the growth and success of the company</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>6-Month Accomplishments:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Independently handle trained cases with efficiency and accuracy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide resolutions based on guidelines and policies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meet daily case goals on a consistent basis</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>12+ Month Accomplishments:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Navigate assigned Tier cases with ease</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Absorbed tier knowledge without depending on resources</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meeting and or exceeding all performance metrics</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT POSHMARK\n\n\nPoshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection. Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.\n\n \n\nPoshmark is the largest community marketplace for fashion where anyone can buy, sell and share their personal style. With millions of shoppers and seller stylists, Poshmark brings together a vibrant community every day to express themselves and share their love of fashion.\n\n \n\nAs a Community Associate, Disputes you are responsible for providing front-line customer support to our growing Community.  You will triage and respond to high volumes of time-sensitive customer inquiries--related to orders, their account, and provide detailed product education.  Our goal is to maintain a high level of customer satisfaction while assisting with a seamless user experience. Your ability to investigate, resolve issues, and communicate effectively will be critical in maintaining Poshmark’s high standards of customer satisfaction.\n\n \n\nThe ideal Community Associate...\n\n - understands empathy is the key to helping others\n\n - exercises strong problem-solving skills\n\n - showcases endless patience and contagious positive energy\n\n - has excellent written and verbal English communication skills\n\n - Is self motivated and thrives working independently.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n - Engage with Poshmark users regarding dispute cases via email support\n\n - Investigate all aspects of an order and find resolutions for dispute cases filed by buyers\n\n - Respond to users in a timely, friendly, and professional manner\n\n - Execute decisions to fairly resolve disputes following Poshmark’s return policies\n\n - Communicate with Poshmark users in a friendly, helpful, and patient manner via email\n\n - Gather feedback and suggestions from the Community\n\n - Strive to exceed Volume, First Response Time, Resolution Rate and CES (Customer Effort Score) goals\n\n - Flexibility to work on holidays and occasional overtime, as required.\n\n \n\nRequirements:\n\n - Overnight shift: 7:30pm/9:30pm/11:30pm  Sun-Thurs/Tues-Sat/Fri-Tues\n\n - AUS shift: 3:30am IST  Sun-Thurs/Tues-Sat/Fri-Tues\n\n - 0-3 years of equivalent experience in customer service or community support, particularly in e-commerce. Customer service via email using Salesforce or previous support experience dealing with US-Based customers preferred; new college graduates are encouraged to apply\n\n - Strong Macbook navigation and typing skills\n\n - Excellent written and verbal English communication skills, with keen attention to detail\n\n - Willing to work on holidays and provide support over weekends, as required\n\n - Problem-solving mindset with the ability to work independently and as part of a team\n\n - Ability to collaborate and interact with managers and peers primarily from the US office headquarters with professionalism\n\n - Enthusiastic about community, customer service, and spreading love and kindness\n\n - Endless patience and a positive attitude with the ability to turn a negative into a positive.\n\n - Competitive by nature; thrives off the success of a team\n\n - Believes that helping users is crucial to the growth and success of the company\n\n \n\n6-Month Accomplishments:\n\n - Independently handle trained cases with efficiency and accuracy\n\n - Provide resolutions based on guidelines and policies\n\n - Meet daily case goals on a consistent basis\n\n \n\n12+ Month Accomplishments:\n\n - Navigate assigned Tier cases with ease\n\n - Absorbed tier knowledge without depending on resources\n\n - Meeting and or exceeding all performance metrics"},{"id":"b13d536d-bb05-4173-a17d-6ed55a2991c7","title":"Staff Engineer, Machine Learning","department":"All Departments","team":"AI/ML Team","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"IN Tamil Nadu (Chennai) - Office","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-23T11:26:14.239+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"India","addressLocality":"Chennai"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/b13d536d-bb05-4173-a17d-6ed55a2991c7","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/b13d536d-bb05-4173-a17d-6ed55a2991c7/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Poshmark</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Poshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection.</strong> Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h1>Staff Engineer Machine Learning</h1><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Big Data team is a central player in the Poshmark organization. Our mission is to build a world-class big data platform to bring value out of data for us and for our customers. Our goal is to democratize data, support exploding business, build data and ML pipelines to fuel existing and new business critical initiatives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for exceptional, creative and passionate Machine Learning engineers to join our ML and Big Data Team. You will be responsible for building and owning the next-generation of algorithms and systems that would have critical business impact for Poshmark and improve the user experience for our millions of users</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explore large datasets, research and develop algorithms/models to solve interesting business problems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and code highly scalable, machine learning applications processing large volumes of data.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate  with multiple teams - data science, business, engineering and help deliver Machine learning based Data products across the company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop best practices and tools to enable robust delivery of features</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and improve architecture in order to ensure horizontal scalability at all layers</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p><h3><strong>Ideal Candidate</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong background in Machine Learning with deep understanding of algorithms and modeling techniques</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of overall software development experience with at least 5+ years  of industry experience applying Machine Learning to concrete problems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Great coding skills and strong software development experience with Big Data technologies &amp; Machine Learning frameworks like SparkML, TensorFlow, PyTorch, Keras</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understanding of distributed systems, and large scale engineering challenges is plus.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h3><strong>Technologies we use</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Scala, Python</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">MongoDB, Redshift, Druid</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Airflow, Jenkins</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Spark, SparkML, Kinesis</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why Poshmark?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Poshmark is a leading social commerce platform for the next generation of retailers and shoppers. Through technology, our mission is to build the world’s most connected shopping experience, while empowering people to build thriving retail businesses.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><br /><br /><br /><br /><br /><br /></p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT POSHMARK\n\n\nPoshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection. Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.\n\n \n\n\nSTAFF ENGINEER MACHINE LEARNING\n\n\n\nBig Data team is a central player in the Poshmark organization. Our mission is to build a world-class big data platform to bring value out of data for us and for our customers. Our goal is to democratize data, support exploding business, build data and ML pipelines to fuel existing and new business critical initiatives.\n\nWe are looking for exceptional, creative and passionate Machine Learning engineers to join our ML and Big Data Team. You will be responsible for building and owning the next-generation of algorithms and systems that would have critical business impact for Poshmark and improve the user experience for our millions of users\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Explore large datasets, research and develop algorithms/models to solve interesting business problems.\n\n - Design and code highly scalable, machine learning applications processing large volumes of data.\n\n - Collaborate  with multiple teams - data science, business, engineering and help deliver Machine learning based Data products across the company.\n\n - Develop best practices and tools to enable robust delivery of features\n\n - Design and improve architecture in order to ensure horizontal scalability at all layers\n\n\n\n\n\nIDEAL CANDIDATE\n\n - Strong background in Machine Learning with deep understanding of algorithms and modeling techniques\n\n - 8+ years of overall software development experience with at least 5+ years  of industry experience applying Machine Learning to concrete problems\n\n - Great coding skills and strong software development experience with Big Data technologies & Machine Learning frameworks like SparkML, TensorFlow, PyTorch, Keras\n\n - Understanding of distributed systems, and large scale engineering challenges is plus.\n\n\n\n\nTECHNOLOGIES WE USE\n\n - Scala, Python\n\n - MongoDB, Redshift, Druid\n\n - Airflow, Jenkins\n\n - Spark, SparkML, Kinesis\n\n\n\nWhy Poshmark?\n\nPoshmark is a leading social commerce platform for the next generation of retailers and shoppers. Through technology, our mission is to build the world’s most connected shopping experience, while empowering people to build thriving retail businesses.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"id":"121f59b9-a44b-4173-8c59-db3e65428ede","title":"Senior Revenue Accountant ","department":"All Departments","team":"Revenue Accounting Team","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"US California (Redwood City) - Office","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-11T23:19:30.508+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Redwood City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/121f59b9-a44b-4173-8c59-db3e65428ede","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/121f59b9-a44b-4173-8c59-db3e65428ede/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Poshmark</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Poshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection.</strong> Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the Role</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Poshmark is seeking a Senior Revenue Accountant to join our Revenue Accounting team. This role requires excellent business, communication, and analytical skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively across functions.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ideal candidate is a self-starter who is comfortable with ambiguity, has strong attention to detail, and is eager to learn complex processes and systems. You take ownership of your work, focus on the fine points, and see daily challenges as opportunities to grow alongside the company.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a high-volume role that requires a hardworking, detail-oriented professional with exceptional communication skills. You'll partner daily with Finance Systems, Engineering, Business Development, Marketing, and Operations teams on various aspects of accounting, including month-end close processes, reconciliations and related analysis, external audit support, monthly/quarterly controls, reporting packages, and ad hoc projects and assignments.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Perform monthly/quarterly revenue accounting close activities, including revenue analysis, journal entries, and account reconciliations for revenue and related accounts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Execute monthly/quarterly Order-to-Cash controls across all revenue streams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reconcile transactions across multiple systems, including subledgers, business intelligence platform, and the ERP system.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with cross-functional teams to investigate and resolve daily inquiries on unusual revenue transactions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with the Finance Systems, Data, and Engineering teams to support system enhancements, API implementations, and process automation related to revenue processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reconcile internal and external data to posted accounting balances, performing complex Order-to-Cash reconciliations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support the implementation of new product and marketing program launches, including system configuration and testing, ensuring compliance with ASC 606.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with SOX implementation and maintain compliance with SOX 404 controls.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support internal and external audits, as well as ad hoc projects as needed<br /></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Requirements:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bachelor's degree in Accounting or equivalent; CPA highly recommended.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of current GAAP standards, including familiarity with ASC 606; Big 4 experience, eCommerce experience, and high-volume transaction experience all preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3–5+ years of Order-to-Cash, revenue, or related accounting experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Public company and SOX 404 experience desired.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with revenue recognition software (Leapfin) and BI tool (Looker)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with NetSuite or an equivalent ERP system; comfortable working through system implementations, integrations, or process automation projects.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Tech-savvy and genuinely curious about how systems and data flow together — quick to pick up new tools, platforms, and AI-driven solutions to streamline accounting processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advanced Excel skills and proficiency in MS Office; actively looks for ways to automate manual work using available AI tools and technology.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail with excellent reconciliation skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational and time management skills, with the ability to prioritize, multitask, and deliver results in a fast-paced environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to think outside the box, work independently with general supervision, and contribute beyond the defined role as business needs require; proactively identifies opportunities for process improvement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Internally motivated to seek out answers, generate ideas, and learn quickly in a fast-paced environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and oral communication skills, with the ability to work effectively as part of a team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">High degree of confidentiality, integrity, and judgment </p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT POSHMARK\n\n\nPoshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection. Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.\n\n \n\nAbout the Role\n\nPoshmark is seeking a Senior Revenue Accountant to join our Revenue Accounting team. This role requires excellent business, communication, and analytical skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively across functions.\n\nThe ideal candidate is a self-starter who is comfortable with ambiguity, has strong attention to detail, and is eager to learn complex processes and systems. You take ownership of your work, focus on the fine points, and see daily challenges as opportunities to grow alongside the company.\n\nThis is a high-volume role that requires a hardworking, detail-oriented professional with exceptional communication skills. You'll partner daily with Finance Systems, Engineering, Business Development, Marketing, and Operations teams on various aspects of accounting, including month-end close processes, reconciliations and related analysis, external audit support, monthly/quarterly controls, reporting packages, and ad hoc projects and assignments.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n - Perform monthly/quarterly revenue accounting close activities, including revenue analysis, journal entries, and account reconciliations for revenue and related accounts.\n\n - Execute monthly/quarterly Order-to-Cash controls across all revenue streams.\n\n - Reconcile transactions across multiple systems, including subledgers, business intelligence platform, and the ERP system.\n\n - Partner with cross-functional teams to investigate and resolve daily inquiries on unusual revenue transactions.\n\n - Collaborate with the Finance Systems, Data, and Engineering teams to support system enhancements, API implementations, and process automation related to revenue processes.\n\n - Reconcile internal and external data to posted accounting balances, performing complex Order-to-Cash reconciliations.\n\n - Support the implementation of new product and marketing program launches, including system configuration and testing, ensuring compliance with ASC 606.\n\n - Assist with SOX implementation and maintain compliance with SOX 404 controls.\n\n - Support internal and external audits, as well as ad hoc projects as needed\n   \n\nRequirements:\n\n - Bachelor's degree in Accounting or equivalent; CPA highly recommended.\n\n - Working knowledge of current GAAP standards, including familiarity with ASC 606; Big 4 experience, eCommerce experience, and high-volume transaction experience all preferred.\n\n - 3–5+ years of Order-to-Cash, revenue, or related accounting experience.\n\n - Public company and SOX 404 experience desired.\n\n - Experience with revenue recognition software (Leapfin) and BI tool (Looker)\n\n - Experience with NetSuite or an equivalent ERP system; comfortable working through system implementations, integrations, or process automation projects.\n\n - Tech-savvy and genuinely curious about how systems and data flow together — quick to pick up new tools, platforms, and AI-driven solutions to streamline accounting processes.\n\n - Advanced Excel skills and proficiency in MS Office; actively looks for ways to automate manual work using available AI tools and technology.\n\n - Strong attention to detail with excellent reconciliation skills.\n\n - Strong organizational and time management skills, with the ability to prioritize, multitask, and deliver results in a fast-paced environment.\n\n - Ability to think outside the box, work independently with general supervision, and contribute beyond the defined role as business needs require; proactively identifies opportunities for process improvement.\n\n - Internally motivated to seek out answers, generate ideas, and learn quickly in a fast-paced environment.\n\n - Strong written and oral communication skills, with the ability to work effectively as part of a team.\n\n - High degree of confidentiality, integrity, and judgment "},{"id":"44f1abe4-3923-4d99-9834-d2a26853ff8f","title":"AML Associate  ","department":"All Departments","team":"Fraud & Risk","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Chennai, Tamil Nadu, India","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-10-15T10:25:43.989+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"postalCode":"600031","addressRegion":"Tamil Nadu","streetAddress":"3rd Floor South Wing, KRM Plaza, Harrington Rd, Chetpet","addressCountry":"India","addressLocality":"Chennai"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/44f1abe4-3923-4d99-9834-d2a26853ff8f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/44f1abe4-3923-4d99-9834-d2a26853ff8f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Poshmark</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Poshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection.</strong> Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Poshmark is looking for an Associate of Financial Crimes Compliance..  This role will report to the Manager of Financial Crimes Compliance.  This exciting role is focused on preventing money laundering in the Poshmark platform and helps Poshmark stay compliant with our Customer Identification Program.  In this community facing role you will have the opportunity to protect Poshmark while ensuring the best experience for the community of users. This position will sit within a growing department at Poshmark and offers opportunity for growth and advancement. You’ll gain deep expertise in a growing field that can turn into a very meaningful career. <br /><br /><strong>Responsibilities</strong><br /><br /><strong>AML and OFAC Knowledge and Application</strong>:  Apply AML best practices. Ensure compliance with KYC and OFAC screening policies. Stay informed and adhere to Poshmark's operational policies. <br /><br /><strong>Quality Control and Accuracy</strong>: Maintain quality standards in decision-making during user reviews. Maintain accurate documentation and reporting.<br /><br /><strong>Teamwork and Communication</strong>: Collaborate effectively with team members. Ensure quality customer communication. Communicate high risk review details to leadership.<br /><br /><strong>6-month accomplishments:</strong></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understand and keep up to date with Poshmark operational policies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Informed on AML program  processes and systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working knowledge of AML best practices</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review accounts to ensure compliance with our identity and sanction screening policies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain quality and accuracy standards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain queues within SLAs (service level agreement)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be a team player - collaborate with other team members to help the team meet their goals and objectives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ensure team communication with customers meet quality standards</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate details of high risk review to team leads and managers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain documentation and reporting requirements for an AML program as outlined by leadership.<br /></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>12+ month accomplishments:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review Low + Medium risk accounts for money laundering or criminal activity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Become a subject matter expert in Poshmark AML topics<br /></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Requirements and skills</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience Requirements - Candidates with 6 Months - 1 year(s) of experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrate strong critical thinking, analytical and decision making skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexibility in shifting priorities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A commitment to protecting Poshmark and it’s community of users</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to understand and communicate complex cases with leadership</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience operating at a high level of professionalism, integrity and discretion</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work independently</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous AML or fraud experience preferred but not required<br /><br /><strong>Work Schedule </strong>: <br />Shift days: <strong>Tuesday - Saturday (or) Sunday - Thursday <br />Time ( IST ) : 7:30pm - 4:30 AM or 4:00 AM to 1 PM</strong></p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT POSHMARK\n\n\nPoshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection. Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.\n\n \n\nPoshmark is looking for an Associate of Financial Crimes Compliance..  This role will report to the Manager of Financial Crimes Compliance.  This exciting role is focused on preventing money laundering in the Poshmark platform and helps Poshmark stay compliant with our Customer Identification Program.  In this community facing role you will have the opportunity to protect Poshmark while ensuring the best experience for the community of users. This position will sit within a growing department at Poshmark and offers opportunity for growth and advancement. You’ll gain deep expertise in a growing field that can turn into a very meaningful career. \n\nResponsibilities\n\nAML and OFAC Knowledge and Application:  Apply AML best practices. Ensure compliance with KYC and OFAC screening policies. Stay informed and adhere to Poshmark's operational policies. \n\nQuality Control and Accuracy: Maintain quality standards in decision-making during user reviews. Maintain accurate documentation and reporting.\n\nTeamwork and Communication: Collaborate effectively with team members. Ensure quality customer communication. Communicate high risk review details to leadership.\n\n6-month accomplishments:\n\n \n\n - Understand and keep up to date with Poshmark operational policies\n\n - Informed on AML program  processes and systems\n\n - Working knowledge of AML best practices\n\n - Review accounts to ensure compliance with our identity and sanction screening policies.\n\n - Maintain quality and accuracy standards\n\n - Maintain queues within SLAs (service level agreement)\n\n - Be a team player - collaborate with other team members to help the team meet their goals and objectives.\n\n - Ensure team communication with customers meet quality standards\n\n - Communicate details of high risk review to team leads and managers.\n\n - Maintain documentation and reporting requirements for an AML program as outlined by leadership.\n   \n\n12+ month accomplishments:\n\n - Review Low + Medium risk accounts for money laundering or criminal activity.\n\n - Become a subject matter expert in Poshmark AML topics\n   \n\nRequirements and skills\n\n - Experience Requirements - Candidates with 6 Months - 1 year(s) of experience\n\n - Demonstrate strong critical thinking, analytical and decision making skills\n\n - Strong communication skills\n\n - Flexibility in shifting priorities\n\n - A commitment to protecting Poshmark and it’s community of users\n\n - Ability to understand and communicate complex cases with leadership\n\n - Experience operating at a high level of professionalism, integrity and discretion\n\n - Ability to work independently\n\n - Previous AML or fraud experience preferred but not required\n   \n   Work Schedule : \n   Shift days: Tuesday - Saturday (or) Sunday - Thursday \n   Time ( IST ) : 7:30pm - 4:30 AM or 4:00 AM to 1 PM"},{"id":"1fbae967-70ba-4139-853b-e5ca749c7aac","title":"Director of Engineering, Growth","department":"All Departments","team":"Core Engineering Team","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"US California (Redwood City) - Office","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-10-05T16:55:44.985+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Redwood City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/1fbae967-70ba-4139-853b-e5ca749c7aac","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/1fbae967-70ba-4139-853b-e5ca749c7aac/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Poshmark</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Poshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection.</strong> Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><h2><strong>About the Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Growth Engineering team builds experiences and platforms that drive sustainable growth across the Poshmark marketplace. The team works across the customer journey—from acquisition and onboarding to engagement, retention, and reactivation—using technology, data, and experimentation to create meaningful customer and business impact.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Growth Engineering operates in highly collaborative, cross-functional squads, partnering closely with Product, Design, Data Science, Analytics, Marketing, and other engineering teams.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As <strong>Director of Engineering (Growth)</strong>, you will lead multiple engineering teams and managers responsible for critical growth initiatives across Poshmark. You will shape the technical strategy, build strong engineering leaders, and create a culture focused on customer outcomes, experimentation, execution, and engineering excellence.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is not a pure management role. We expect our Directors to have the technical depth to engage in architecture discussions, challenge technical decisions, and help teams navigate complex technical and product problems.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead multiple engineering teams and Engineering Managers across the Growth organization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Product, Design, Data Science, Analytics, and Marketing to define Growth strategy, roadmaps, and priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive measurable improvements across acquisition, activation, engagement, retention, and other key growth opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build a strong experimentation culture, enabling teams to rapidly test, learn, iterate, and scale successful ideas.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive execution across complex, cross-functional initiatives while improving predictability and time-to-market.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop Engineering Managers, senior technical leaders, and future leaders across the organization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and evolve the technical strategy and architecture needed to support Poshmark's long-term growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain a high bar for engineering excellence, including automated testing, CI/CD, observability, reliability, performance, and operational ownership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Champion incremental development and frequent production deployments, enabling teams to learn and deliver value quickly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Balance product delivery with investments in technical health, scalability, developer productivity, and platform modernization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own organizational planning, staffing, hiring, talent development, and succession planning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Foster a high-performing engineering culture built around clear ownership, accountability, collaboration, continuous improvement, and end-to-end ownership.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Requirements</strong></h2><h3><strong>Required</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">15+ years of software engineering experience, with significant experience building high-scale consumer products or distributed systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">7+ years of engineering leadership experience, including experience leading Engineering Managers and multiple engineering teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proven track record delivering complex, high-impact product and technology initiatives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong technical depth with the ability to participate meaningfully in architecture, system design, and technical strategy discussions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building experimentation-driven products and using data to make product and engineering decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to partner effectively with Product, Design, Data Science, Analytics, Marketing, and other business functions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of modern engineering practices, including automated testing, CI/CD, observability, reliability, and scalable system design.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience developing engineering leaders and building high-performing teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills with the ability to influence senior technical, product, and executive stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to operate effectively in a fast-moving environment with ambiguity and evolving priorities.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Preferred</strong></h3><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience leading <strong>Growth Engineering</strong> in marketplaces, e-commerce, social, or other high-scale consumer products, including globally distributed teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with <strong>Customer Data Platforms (CDPs) and MarTech ecosystems</strong>, including segmentation, lifecycle marketing, personalization, attribution, analytics, and cross-channel activation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building and scaling <strong>experimentation, personalization, and AI/ML-driven growth capabilities</strong> to improve customer acquisition, engagement, and retention.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated success driving <strong>engineering and organizational transformation</strong>, including modernizing platforms, practices, and ways of working.</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT POSHMARK\n\n\nPoshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection. Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.\n\n \n\n\nABOUT THE TEAM\n\nThe Growth Engineering team builds experiences and platforms that drive sustainable growth across the Poshmark marketplace. The team works across the customer journey—from acquisition and onboarding to engagement, retention, and reactivation—using technology, data, and experimentation to create meaningful customer and business impact.\n\nGrowth Engineering operates in highly collaborative, cross-functional squads, partnering closely with Product, Design, Data Science, Analytics, Marketing, and other engineering teams.\n\nAs Director of Engineering (Growth), you will lead multiple engineering teams and managers responsible for critical growth initiatives across Poshmark. You will shape the technical strategy, build strong engineering leaders, and create a culture focused on customer outcomes, experimentation, execution, and engineering excellence.\n\nThis is not a pure management role. We expect our Directors to have the technical depth to engage in architecture discussions, challenge technical decisions, and help teams navigate complex technical and product problems.\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Lead multiple engineering teams and Engineering Managers across the Growth organization.\n\n - Partner with Product, Design, Data Science, Analytics, and Marketing to define Growth strategy, roadmaps, and priorities.\n\n - Drive measurable improvements across acquisition, activation, engagement, retention, and other key growth opportunities.\n\n - Build a strong experimentation culture, enabling teams to rapidly test, learn, iterate, and scale successful ideas.\n\n - Drive execution across complex, cross-functional initiatives while improving predictability and time-to-market.\n\n - Develop Engineering Managers, senior technical leaders, and future leaders across the organization.\n\n - Define and evolve the technical strategy and architecture needed to support Poshmark's long-term growth.\n\n - Maintain a high bar for engineering excellence, including automated testing, CI/CD, observability, reliability, performance, and operational ownership.\n\n - Champion incremental development and frequent production deployments, enabling teams to learn and deliver value quickly.\n\n - Balance product delivery with investments in technical health, scalability, developer productivity, and platform modernization.\n\n - Own organizational planning, staffing, hiring, talent development, and succession planning.\n\n - Foster a high-performing engineering culture built around clear ownership, accountability, collaboration, continuous improvement, and end-to-end ownership.\n\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n\n\nREQUIRED\n\n - 15+ years of software engineering experience, with significant experience building high-scale consumer products or distributed systems.\n\n - 7+ years of engineering leadership experience, including experience leading Engineering Managers and multiple engineering teams.\n\n - Proven track record delivering complex, high-impact product and technology initiatives.\n\n - Strong technical depth with the ability to participate meaningfully in architecture, system design, and technical strategy discussions.\n\n - Experience building experimentation-driven products and using data to make product and engineering decisions.\n\n - Demonstrated ability to partner effectively with Product, Design, Data Science, Analytics, Marketing, and other business functions.\n\n - Strong understanding of modern engineering practices, including automated testing, CI/CD, observability, reliability, and scalable system design.\n\n - Experience developing engineering leaders and building high-performing teams.\n\n - Strong communication skills with the ability to influence senior technical, product, and executive stakeholders.\n\n - Ability to operate effectively in a fast-moving environment with ambiguity and evolving priorities.\n\n\nPREFERRED\n\n - Experience leading Growth Engineering in marketplaces, e-commerce, social, or other high-scale consumer products, including globally distributed teams.\n\n - Experience with Customer Data Platforms (CDPs) and MarTech ecosystems, including segmentation, lifecycle marketing, personalization, attribution, analytics, and cross-channel activation.\n\n - Experience building and scaling experimentation, personalization, and AI/ML-driven growth capabilities to improve customer acquisition, engagement, and retention.\n\n - Demonstrated success driving engineering and organizational transformation, including modernizing platforms, practices, and ways of working."},{"id":"016b4d63-97b3-4ba4-8555-b4565f1bb157","title":"Live E-Commerce Digital Host","department":"All Departments","team":"Consignment Solutions Team","employmentType":"PartTime","location":"US Pennsylvania (Philadelphia) - Office","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-10-08T19:30:53.113+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Pennsylvania","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Philadelphia"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/016b4d63-97b3-4ba4-8555-b4565f1bb157","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/016b4d63-97b3-4ba4-8555-b4565f1bb157/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Poshmark</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Poshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection.</strong> Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Live E-Commerce Digital Host:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Digital Host represents our brand on camera during live e-commerce shows, engaging directly with shoppers and driving sales through confident, knowledgeable product presentations. This role combines fashion expertise, sales ability, and on-camera presence to create an engaging shopping experience and help grow Live as a key sales channel.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Host live shopping shows on-site using the Poshmark Live platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Present fashion and luxury products clearly, confidently, and accurately.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engage with viewers in real time by answering questions, responding to comments, and creating an interactive shopping experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Drive sales through product storytelling, strong calls to action, and appropriate urgency.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Speak knowledgeably about contemporary, designer, and luxury brands, including product features, materials, trends, and value.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with the Console Coordinator to maintain show pacing, organization, and momentum.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adapt presentation and selling approach based on audience engagement and show performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with the Live team to prepare products and priorities for each show.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain a professional, engaging, and consistent brand presence on camera.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Assist with post-show feedback and identify opportunities to improve future live events.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>6-Month Accomplishments:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Within the first six months, a successful Digital Host will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Independently host a standard Live show from start to finish with minimal supervision.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrate confidence and a natural, engaging presence on camera.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop a strong understanding of the Live workflow and work effectively with the Console Coordinator throughout each show.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrate strong working knowledge of the brands, products, terminology, and key selling points needed for assigned shows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Present products accurately while keeping the show moving at an appropriate pace.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Effectively engage viewers, respond to questions, and encourage participation and purchasing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use product storytelling, urgency, and calls to action naturally to support sales.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Read audience engagement and adjust energy, pacing, or selling approach when needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understand Poshmark-specific policies and processes that impact the buyer experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be reliable and prepared for assigned Live shifts and trusted to independently host standard shows.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>12+ Month Accomplishments:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">After 12 months, a successful Digital Host will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Confidently host a variety of Live formats, including luxury, outlet, high-volume, weekend, and special-event shows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrate strong product and brand knowledge across a broad range of categories.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adapt selling style based on the audience, merchandise, show format, and real-time performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Consistently create an engaging shopping experience while maintaining strong show pacing and sales focus.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Recognize when a show needs to speed up, slow down, change direction, or adjust its selling approach.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work seamlessly with Console Coordinators and anticipate operational needs during the stream.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Handle unexpected situations or changes during a Live professionally without disrupting the buyer experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use experience from prior shows to identify opportunities to improve engagement and sales performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide useful feedback on product selection, show structure, and other opportunities to strengthen Live performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a resource for newer hosts and support training or shadowing when needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be trusted to host high-priority or challenging Live events with minimal supervision.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Requirements:<br /></strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong knowledge of contemporary and luxury fashion brands.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Genuine interest in fashion, designers, products, and current trends.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable speaking on camera and engaging with a live audience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong verbal communication and interpersonal skills.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Sales-oriented mindset with the ability to engage, persuade, and create excitement around products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to think quickly and adapt based on audience response and live show needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable learning and using live-streaming technology and related systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and ability to communicate product information accurately.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional, dependable, punctual, and prepared for scheduled shows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to collaborate effectively with Console Coordinators and other members of the Live team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in live selling, hosting, broadcasting, fashion retail, luxury goods, e-commerce, or another customer-facing sales role preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Availability to work on-site at our location in Northeast Philadelphia for daytime, evening, and weekend Live shifts based on business needs.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT POSHMARK\n\n\nPoshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection. Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.\n\n \n\nLive E-Commerce Digital Host:\n\nThe Digital Host represents our brand on camera during live e-commerce shows, engaging directly with shoppers and driving sales through confident, knowledgeable product presentations. This role combines fashion expertise, sales ability, and on-camera presence to create an engaging shopping experience and help grow Live as a key sales channel.\n\n\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n - Host live shopping shows on-site using the Poshmark Live platform.\n\n - Present fashion and luxury products clearly, confidently, and accurately.\n\n - Engage with viewers in real time by answering questions, responding to comments, and creating an interactive shopping experience.\n\n - Drive sales through product storytelling, strong calls to action, and appropriate urgency.\n\n - Speak knowledgeably about contemporary, designer, and luxury brands, including product features, materials, trends, and value.\n\n - Partner closely with the Console Coordinator to maintain show pacing, organization, and momentum.\n\n - Adapt presentation and selling approach based on audience engagement and show performance.\n\n - Collaborate with the Live team to prepare products and priorities for each show.\n\n - Maintain a professional, engaging, and consistent brand presence on camera.\n\n - Assist with post-show feedback and identify opportunities to improve future live events.\n   \n   \n\n6-Month Accomplishments:\n\nWithin the first six months, a successful Digital Host will:\n\n - Independently host a standard Live show from start to finish with minimal supervision.\n\n - Demonstrate confidence and a natural, engaging presence on camera.\n\n - Develop a strong understanding of the Live workflow and work effectively with the Console Coordinator throughout each show.\n\n - Demonstrate strong working knowledge of the brands, products, terminology, and key selling points needed for assigned shows.\n\n - Present products accurately while keeping the show moving at an appropriate pace.\n\n - Effectively engage viewers, respond to questions, and encourage participation and purchasing.\n\n - Use product storytelling, urgency, and calls to action naturally to support sales.\n\n - Read audience engagement and adjust energy, pacing, or selling approach when needed.\n\n - Understand Poshmark-specific policies and processes that impact the buyer experience.\n\n - Be reliable and prepared for assigned Live shifts and trusted to independently host standard shows.\n\n\n\n12+ Month Accomplishments:\n\nAfter 12 months, a successful Digital Host will:\n\n - Confidently host a variety of Live formats, including luxury, outlet, high-volume, weekend, and special-event shows.\n\n - Demonstrate strong product and brand knowledge across a broad range of categories.\n\n - Adapt selling style based on the audience, merchandise, show format, and real-time performance.\n\n - Consistently create an engaging shopping experience while maintaining strong show pacing and sales focus.\n\n - Recognize when a show needs to speed up, slow down, change direction, or adjust its selling approach.\n\n - Work seamlessly with Console Coordinators and anticipate operational needs during the stream.\n\n - Handle unexpected situations or changes during a Live professionally without disrupting the buyer experience.\n\n - Use experience from prior shows to identify opportunities to improve engagement and sales performance.\n\n - Provide useful feedback on product selection, show structure, and other opportunities to strengthen Live performance.\n\n - Serve as a resource for newer hosts and support training or shadowing when needed.\n\n - Be trusted to host high-priority or challenging Live events with minimal supervision.\n   \n   \n\nRequirements:\n\n\n - Strong knowledge of contemporary and luxury fashion brands.\n\n - Genuine interest in fashion, designers, products, and current trends.\n\n - Comfortable speaking on camera and engaging with a live audience.\n\n - Strong verbal communication and interpersonal skills.\n\n - Sales-oriented mindset with the ability to engage, persuade, and create excitement around products.\n\n - Ability to think quickly and adapt based on audience response and live show needs.\n\n - Comfortable learning and using live-streaming technology and related systems.\n\n - Strong attention to detail and ability to communicate product information accurately.\n\n - Professional, dependable, punctual, and prepared for scheduled shows.\n\n - Ability to collaborate effectively with Console Coordinators and other members of the Live team.\n\n - Experience in live selling, hosting, broadcasting, fashion retail, luxury goods, e-commerce, or another customer-facing sales role preferred.\n\n - Availability to work on-site at our location in Northeast Philadelphia for daytime, evening, and weekend Live shifts based on business needs.\n\n\n"},{"id":"1e779262-dc7d-423f-9aae-a31ab923167c","title":"Sr. Manager, Enterprise Development","department":"All Departments","team":"Enterprise Seller Team","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"US California (Redwood City) - Office","secondaryLocations":[{"location":"US New York (New York) - Office","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-11-05T18:39:56.875+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Redwood City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/1e779262-dc7d-423f-9aae-a31ab923167c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/1e779262-dc7d-423f-9aae-a31ab923167c/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Poshmark</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Poshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection.</strong> Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Poshmark is looking for an Enterprise Business Development Manager to grow high-quality seller supply and inventory across Posh Live and the broader Poshmark marketplace.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role will be primarily responsible for identifying, pitching, and onboarding enterprise sellers for Posh Live, while helping them build a successful and scalable presence across Poshmark. You will partner with sellers to develop the right commercial strategy for their business—using live shopping, catalog, and assortment opportunities to reach customers, grow sales, and create long-term value on the platform.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will be a strategic, commercially minded relationship builder who understands how to win and grow enterprise partnerships in a two-sided marketplace.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Source, evaluate, and close high-potential enterprise sellers, brands, retailers, liquidators, and other supply partners for Posh Live and Poshmark.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and manage a pipeline of prospective partners, from initial outreach and pitch through contracting, onboarding, launch, and long-term account growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead with Posh Live as a key acquisition opportunity, helping partners understand how live selling can drive discovery, engagement, and conversion.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop tailored partner strategies that combine live shows with catalog selling, assortment planning, and ongoing marketplace growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advise partners on merchandising, pricing, inventory selection, show formats, and operational best practices to maximize performance across channels.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with Partner Success, Host Growth, Product, Marketing, Operations, and Legal to ensure partners launch successfully and are set up for sustained growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track partner performance and identify opportunities to improve GMV, sell-through, repeat participation, catalog adoption, and overall account health.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bring market intelligence back to the team, including insights on seller needs, competitive dynamics, categories, and emerging supply opportunities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help shape the enterprise seller value proposition and scalable playbooks for acquiring and growing high-value partners.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Bring</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of business development, partnerships, sales, account management, or marketplace experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated experience sourcing and closing complex commercial partnerships, ideally with brands, retailers, sellers, creators, or supply partners.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong commercial judgment and comfort negotiating partnership terms, evaluating opportunity size, and managing a sales pipeline.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A deep understanding of e-commerce, marketplaces, resale, retail, live commerce, or social commerce.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to build credibility with senior external partners and translate their business needs into a compelling Poshmark growth strategy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong analytical skills and a habit of using data to identify opportunities, diagnose performance, and prioritize action.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent cross-functional collaboration skills and the ability to drive execution across multiple internal teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Entrepreneurial mindset, high ownership, and comfort building new programs in a fast-moving environment.</p></li></ul><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice to Hav</strong>e</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in live commerce, creator commerce, fashion, resale, off-price retail, or liquidation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Existing relationships with enterprise sellers, brands, retailers, or live commerce operators.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience managing both acquisition and post-close growth for strategic accounts.</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT POSHMARK\n\n\nPoshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection. Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.\n\n \n\nPoshmark is looking for an Enterprise Business Development Manager to grow high-quality seller supply and inventory across Posh Live and the broader Poshmark marketplace.\n\nThis role will be primarily responsible for identifying, pitching, and onboarding enterprise sellers for Posh Live, while helping them build a successful and scalable presence across Poshmark. You will partner with sellers to develop the right commercial strategy for their business—using live shopping, catalog, and assortment opportunities to reach customers, grow sales, and create long-term value on the platform.\n\n \n\nYou will be a strategic, commercially minded relationship builder who understands how to win and grow enterprise partnerships in a two-sided marketplace.\n\n \n\nWhat You’ll Do\n\n - Source, evaluate, and close high-potential enterprise sellers, brands, retailers, liquidators, and other supply partners for Posh Live and Poshmark.\n\n - Build and manage a pipeline of prospective partners, from initial outreach and pitch through contracting, onboarding, launch, and long-term account growth.\n\n - Lead with Posh Live as a key acquisition opportunity, helping partners understand how live selling can drive discovery, engagement, and conversion.\n\n - Develop tailored partner strategies that combine live shows with catalog selling, assortment planning, and ongoing marketplace growth.\n\n - Advise partners on merchandising, pricing, inventory selection, show formats, and operational best practices to maximize performance across channels.\n\n - Work closely with Partner Success, Host Growth, Product, Marketing, Operations, and Legal to ensure partners launch successfully and are set up for sustained growth.\n\n - Track partner performance and identify opportunities to improve GMV, sell-through, repeat participation, catalog adoption, and overall account health.\n\n - Bring market intelligence back to the team, including insights on seller needs, competitive dynamics, categories, and emerging supply opportunities.\n\n - Help shape the enterprise seller value proposition and scalable playbooks for acquiring and growing high-value partners.\n\nWhat You’ll Bring\n\n - 5+ years of business development, partnerships, sales, account management, or marketplace experience.\n\n - Demonstrated experience sourcing and closing complex commercial partnerships, ideally with brands, retailers, sellers, creators, or supply partners.\n\n - Strong commercial judgment and comfort negotiating partnership terms, evaluating opportunity size, and managing a sales pipeline.\n\n - A deep understanding of e-commerce, marketplaces, resale, retail, live commerce, or social commerce.\n\n - Ability to build credibility with senior external partners and translate their business needs into a compelling Poshmark growth strategy.\n\n - Strong analytical skills and a habit of using data to identify opportunities, diagnose performance, and prioritize action.\n\n - Excellent cross-functional collaboration skills and the ability to drive execution across multiple internal teams.\n\n - Entrepreneurial mindset, high ownership, and comfort building new programs in a fast-moving environment.\n\n \n\nNice to Have\n\n - Experience in live commerce, creator commerce, fashion, resale, off-price retail, or liquidation.\n\n - Existing relationships with enterprise sellers, brands, retailers, or live commerce operators.\n\n - Experience managing both acquisition and post-close growth for strategic accounts."},{"id":"da7b41b5-c116-4187-b51a-10c676afb053","title":"Console Coordinator - Live E-Commerce","department":"All Departments","team":"Consignment Solutions Team","employmentType":"PartTime","location":"US Pennsylvania (Philadelphia) - Office","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-10-08T16:34:40.007+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"Pennsylvania","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Philadelphia"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/da7b41b5-c116-4187-b51a-10c676afb053","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/da7b41b5-c116-4187-b51a-10c676afb053/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Poshmark</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Poshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection.</strong> Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Console Coordinator manages the behind-the-scenes execution of Linda's Stuff's live e-commerce events, working directly with the host to keep each show organized, accurate, and moving at the right pace. This role combines live operations, sales instincts, inventory organization, and real-time problem solving to create strong buyer experience and drive sales. It is an opportunity to play a hands-on role in a fast-growing live commerce channel where decisions made during each stream have an immediate impact on performance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Set up and operate the live selling console from pre-show preparation through post-show wrap-up.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage products during live broadcasts, including pinning items, adjusting pricing, tracking sold inventory, and maintaining accurate SKU organization.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work closely with the host throughout the stream to maintain pacing, momentum, urgency, and an engaging buyer experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Anticipate what the host will need next and keep products and information organized so the stream continues smoothly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monitor audience activity, chat, buyer questions, and sales activity and communicate relevant information to the host in real time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain strong SKU discipline, particularly for mystery items, giveaways, sold inventory, and other products that may require additional tracking after the show.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond to common technical, inventory, and operational issues during live events and escalate issues appropriately when needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adapt quickly when inventory, technology, staffing, or the planned show flow changes unexpectedly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Coordinate with inventory, fulfillment, customer service, and other teams as needed to resolve live and post-live issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Accurately complete required post-live reporting, metrics, and operational follow-up.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow platform and company policies related to bidding, shipping, cancellations, returns, and other live-selling activity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute feedback and ideas that improve live workflows, show execution, and the overall buyer experience.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>6-Month Accomplishments:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Within the first six months, a successful Console Coordinator will:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Independently set up and run the console for a standard live event from start to finish.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understand the full live workflow, including preparation, SKU organization, running items, tracking sales, and post-show wrap-up.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be comfortable navigating the live selling platform and the other systems and tools required during a shift.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Keep the host organized and anticipate upcoming needs rather than relying solely on direction during the stream.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate SKU organization, especially for mystery items, giveaways, sold inventory, and items that could otherwise be difficult to identify after the show.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Recognize common technical and operational issues and confidently complete the appropriate first troubleshooting steps.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate clearly with hosts and the broader Live team when issues arise and know when escalation is necessary.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Effectively manage the console during high-volume or fast-paced periods while maintaining accuracy and show flow.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Understand the key platform and company policies that affect live selling, including bidding, shipping, cancellations, and returns.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Accurately complete required post-live reporting and metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be trusted to independently handle a standard console shift with minimal supervision.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>12+ Month Accomplishments:</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Within the first twelve months, a successful Console Coordinator will:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Confidently run a wide variety of live events, including high-volume, luxury, outlet, weekend, and special-event streams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot most common console, inventory, SKU, and stream issues independently and recognize when an issue requires escalation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Anticipate potential problems and take proactive steps to address them before they affect the host or buyer experience.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Adapt quickly and effectively when inventory, staffing, technology, or the planned stream changes unexpectedly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrate a strong understanding of how console execution impacts the buyer experience, sales performance, shipping, fulfillment, and customer service downstream.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Help the host maintain strong pacing and momentum by recognizing when the stream should speed up, slow down, or pivot based on buyer engagement and sales activity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain exceptional organization of SKUs and sold inventory and consistently prevent avoidable post-stream issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Serve as a knowledgeable resource for newer Console Coordinators and support training or shadowing as needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify inefficiencies and recommend practical improvements to live workflows, tools, and processes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be trusted to independently manage the console for high-priority, complex, or high-volume live events.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrate strong ownership of Live operations and serve as a go-to resource for console-related questions and execution.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Requirements:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in live selling, live streaming, e-commerce operations, digital sales, or a related environment preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong sales instincts and the ability to recognize opportunities to maintain urgency, engagement, and momentum during a live event.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to multitask, prioritize, and make quick decisions in a fast-paced live environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organizational skills and exceptional attention to detail, particularly when managing SKUs, inventory, pricing, and sold items.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Tech-savvy and comfortable learning and navigating multiple platforms and systems.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills and the ability to work closely with hosts and other team members in real time.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to remain composed, adaptable, and solutions-oriented when technical or operational issues arise.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable and able to work independently during assigned broadcasts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to work on-site in Northeast Philadelphia, PA.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Availability for daytime, evening, and weekend shifts based on the live show schedule.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT POSHMARK\n\n\nPoshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection. Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.\n\n \n\nThe Console Coordinator manages the behind-the-scenes execution of Linda's Stuff's live e-commerce events, working directly with the host to keep each show organized, accurate, and moving at the right pace. This role combines live operations, sales instincts, inventory organization, and real-time problem solving to create strong buyer experience and drive sales. It is an opportunity to play a hands-on role in a fast-growing live commerce channel where decisions made during each stream have an immediate impact on performance.\n\n\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n - Set up and operate the live selling console from pre-show preparation through post-show wrap-up.\n\n - Manage products during live broadcasts, including pinning items, adjusting pricing, tracking sold inventory, and maintaining accurate SKU organization.\n\n - Work closely with the host throughout the stream to maintain pacing, momentum, urgency, and an engaging buyer experience.\n\n - Anticipate what the host will need next and keep products and information organized so the stream continues smoothly.\n\n - Monitor audience activity, chat, buyer questions, and sales activity and communicate relevant information to the host in real time.\n\n - Maintain strong SKU discipline, particularly for mystery items, giveaways, sold inventory, and other products that may require additional tracking after the show.\n\n - Respond to common technical, inventory, and operational issues during live events and escalate issues appropriately when needed.\n\n - Adapt quickly when inventory, technology, staffing, or the planned show flow changes unexpectedly.\n\n - Coordinate with inventory, fulfillment, customer service, and other teams as needed to resolve live and post-live issues.\n\n - Accurately complete required post-live reporting, metrics, and operational follow-up.\n\n - Follow platform and company policies related to bidding, shipping, cancellations, returns, and other live-selling activity.\n\n - Contribute feedback and ideas that improve live workflows, show execution, and the overall buyer experience.\n\n\n\n6-Month Accomplishments:\n\nWithin the first six months, a successful Console Coordinator will:\n\n - Independently set up and run the console for a standard live event from start to finish.\n\n - Understand the full live workflow, including preparation, SKU organization, running items, tracking sales, and post-show wrap-up.\n\n - Be comfortable navigating the live selling platform and the other systems and tools required during a shift.\n\n - Keep the host organized and anticipate upcoming needs rather than relying solely on direction during the stream.\n\n - Maintain accurate SKU organization, especially for mystery items, giveaways, sold inventory, and items that could otherwise be difficult to identify after the show.\n\n - Recognize common technical and operational issues and confidently complete the appropriate first troubleshooting steps.\n\n - Communicate clearly with hosts and the broader Live team when issues arise and know when escalation is necessary.\n\n - Effectively manage the console during high-volume or fast-paced periods while maintaining accuracy and show flow.\n\n - Understand the key platform and company policies that affect live selling, including bidding, shipping, cancellations, and returns.\n\n - Accurately complete required post-live reporting and metrics.\n\n - Be trusted to independently handle a standard console shift with minimal supervision.\n\n\n\n\n12+ Month Accomplishments:\n\nWithin the first twelve months, a successful Console Coordinator will:\n\n\n\n - Confidently run a wide variety of live events, including high-volume, luxury, outlet, weekend, and special-event streams.\n\n - Troubleshoot most common console, inventory, SKU, and stream issues independently and recognize when an issue requires escalation.\n\n - Anticipate potential problems and take proactive steps to address them before they affect the host or buyer experience.\n\n - Adapt quickly and effectively when inventory, staffing, technology, or the planned stream changes unexpectedly.\n\n - Demonstrate a strong understanding of how console execution impacts the buyer experience, sales performance, shipping, fulfillment, and customer service downstream.\n\n - Help the host maintain strong pacing and momentum by recognizing when the stream should speed up, slow down, or pivot based on buyer engagement and sales activity.\n\n - Maintain exceptional organization of SKUs and sold inventory and consistently prevent avoidable post-stream issues.\n\n - Serve as a knowledgeable resource for newer Console Coordinators and support training or shadowing as needed.\n\n - Identify inefficiencies and recommend practical improvements to live workflows, tools, and processes.\n\n - Be trusted to independently manage the console for high-priority, complex, or high-volume live events.\n\n - Demonstrate strong ownership of Live operations and serve as a go-to resource for console-related questions and execution.\n\n\n\nRequirements:\n\n - Experience in live selling, live streaming, e-commerce operations, digital sales, or a related environment preferred.\n\n - Strong sales instincts and the ability to recognize opportunities to maintain urgency, engagement, and momentum during a live event.\n\n - Ability to multitask, prioritize, and make quick decisions in a fast-paced live environment.\n\n - Strong organizational skills and exceptional attention to detail, particularly when managing SKUs, inventory, pricing, and sold items.\n\n - Tech-savvy and comfortable learning and navigating multiple platforms and systems.\n\n - Strong communication skills and the ability to work closely with hosts and other team members in real time.\n\n - Ability to remain composed, adaptable, and solutions-oriented when technical or operational issues arise.\n\n - Reliable and able to work independently during assigned broadcasts.\n\n - Ability to work on-site in Northeast Philadelphia, PA.\n\n - Availability for daytime, evening, and weekend shifts based on the live show schedule.\n\n"},{"id":"edec37aa-e736-46f1-94ae-67dda542c8ea","title":"Director, Inventory Management & Planning","department":"All Departments","team":"Merchandising Team","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"US California (Redwood City) - Office","secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-11-07T00:16:34.548+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":null,"workplaceType":null,"address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Redwood City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/edec37aa-e736-46f1-94ae-67dda542c8ea","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/edec37aa-e736-46f1-94ae-67dda542c8ea/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Poshmark</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Poshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection.</strong> Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is critical to building and leading the end-to-end inventory planning and allocation function across Poshmark. You will ensure inventory is optimized across all categories and channels while balancing in-stock performance across Stores, E-commerce, and the Warehouse. As the architect of inventory planning, you will build out the function, strategies, processes, tools, and team needed to support and scale Poshmark. This role reports to the VP of Merchandising.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Responsibilities</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Store Allocation &amp; Warehouse Management</em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop and maintain inventory forecasts for the Distribution Center, Merchandising, Finance, and Store teams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead onboarding, testing, and scaling of the inventory management system for owned and store inventory.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Distribution Center operations to optimize inbound scheduling, storage utilization, and inventory flow.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with Merchandising on store allocations and the timing of new product launches.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage store stock pulls and inventory sendbacks as needed.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Inventory Strategy &amp; Open-to-Buy</em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create and run weekly category- and brand-level reporting to drive deeper merchandising insights.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build a monthly Open-to-Buy for owned inventory that aligns with Store and E-commerce sales budgets and optimizes turn.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own end-to-end inventory for <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Poshmark.com\">Poshmark.com</a>, the warehouse, and store locations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Establish sell-through and weeks-on-hand targets by product type.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track and manage owned inventory and product lifecycle with the Merchandising team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop a markdown cadence, and identify and resolve inventory gluts.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>Cross-Functional Partnership</em></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with the Data Analytics and Tech teams to develop and implement an inventory tracking and forecasting system.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with Merchandising, Store Operations, and Finance to align inventory strategy with business priorities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Represent the planning function to senior leadership, clearly communicating inventory position, risks, and opportunities.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of experience at the senior manager level or above in retail inventory planning or management.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building merchandise planning and inventory management tools and processes from the ground up.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience consolidating data sources into clear, actionable insights.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working with distribution center operations and retail store allocation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Advanced Excel and financial modeling skills, with the ability to turn data into actionable plans.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to navigate ambiguity, anticipate needs, and build frameworks independently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in multi-category retail or DTC environments preferred.</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT POSHMARK\n\n\nPoshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection. Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.\n\n \n\nThis role is critical to building and leading the end-to-end inventory planning and allocation function across Poshmark. You will ensure inventory is optimized across all categories and channels while balancing in-stock performance across Stores, E-commerce, and the Warehouse. As the architect of inventory planning, you will build out the function, strategies, processes, tools, and team needed to support and scale Poshmark. This role reports to the VP of Merchandising.\n\nResponsibilities\n\nStore Allocation & Warehouse Management\n\n - Develop and maintain inventory forecasts for the Distribution Center, Merchandising, Finance, and Store teams.\n\n - Lead onboarding, testing, and scaling of the inventory management system for owned and store inventory.\n\n - Partner with Distribution Center operations to optimize inbound scheduling, storage utilization, and inventory flow.\n\n - Partner with Merchandising on store allocations and the timing of new product launches.\n\n - Manage store stock pulls and inventory sendbacks as needed.\n\nInventory Strategy & Open-to-Buy\n\n - Create and run weekly category- and brand-level reporting to drive deeper merchandising insights.\n\n - Build a monthly Open-to-Buy for owned inventory that aligns with Store and E-commerce sales budgets and optimizes turn.\n\n - Own end-to-end inventory for Poshmark.com http://Poshmark.com, the warehouse, and store locations.\n\n - Establish sell-through and weeks-on-hand targets by product type.\n\n - Track and manage owned inventory and product lifecycle with the Merchandising team.\n\n - Develop a markdown cadence, and identify and resolve inventory gluts.\n\nCross-Functional Partnership\n\n - Partner with the Data Analytics and Tech teams to develop and implement an inventory tracking and forecasting system.\n\n - Collaborate with Merchandising, Store Operations, and Finance to align inventory strategy with business priorities.\n\n - Represent the planning function to senior leadership, clearly communicating inventory position, risks, and opportunities.\n\nRequirements\n\n - 3+ years of experience at the senior manager level or above in retail inventory planning or management.\n\n - Experience building merchandise planning and inventory management tools and processes from the ground up.\n\n - Experience consolidating data sources into clear, actionable insights.\n\n - Experience working with distribution center operations and retail store allocation.\n\n - Advanced Excel and financial modeling skills, with the ability to turn data into actionable plans.\n\n - Ability to navigate ambiguity, anticipate needs, and build frameworks independently.\n\n - Experience in multi-category retail or DTC environments preferred."},{"id":"5b13d4ca-3dfe-42a3-9e9e-fbd3283e16a3","title":"Senior Host Operations Associate II, Posh Live","department":"All Departments","team":"Seller Product Team","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"US California - Remote","secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Redwood City, California, USA","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Redwood City"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-11-06T22:40:34.619+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Sacramento"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/5b13d4ca-3dfe-42a3-9e9e-fbd3283e16a3","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/poshmark/5b13d4ca-3dfe-42a3-9e9e-fbd3283e16a3/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Poshmark</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /><strong>Poshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection.</strong> Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for a Host Operations Specialist to help our hosts run their day-to-day businesses smoothly and support the growth of Posh Live.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In this role, you’ll own day-to-day host support and coordinate technical issues from initial report through resolution. You’ll work closely with the Account Manager, Product, Engineering, and Customer Support to troubleshoot problems, keep hosts informed, and identify opportunities to improve the host experience.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As Posh Live grows, you’ll help build the processes and resources that allow us to support more hosts effectively.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll do</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Support hosts with everyday questions and issues.</strong> Help hosts navigate product features, show operations, and order-related questions. Resolve issues directly where possible and coordinate with the appropriate teams when additional support is needed.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own bug tracking and follow-up.</strong> Gather details, reproduce issues where possible, and document clear bug reports, including the impact on hosts’ businesses. Track progress with Product and Engineering and follow through until issues are resolved or a clear next step is established.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Keep hosts informed.</strong> Provide timely updates, explain available workarounds, and close the loop when an issue is resolved.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Identify recurring problems.</strong> Look for patterns across host feedback and support requests, and bring actionable recommendations to the team.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Improve how we support hosts.</strong> Maintain troubleshooting guides, FAQs, and escalation processes to make support faster and more consistent.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Partner with the Account Manager.</strong> Coordinate on host needs and escalations, bringing in account context when needed and ensuring clear ownership of next steps.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Contribute to business improvements.</strong> Work closely with the Posh Live team to identify operational friction that affects hosts’ ability to run shows, fulfill orders, and grow their businesses.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you’ll bring</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in customer support, account operations, marketplace operations, or a similar role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong problem-solving skills and comfort troubleshooting product and operational issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong organization and follow-through, with the ability to manage multiple open issues.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear, empathetic communication with hosts and internal partners.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good judgment about urgency, business impact, and when to escalate.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A proactive mindset and willingness to adapt as the business evolves.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with Poshmark; experience supporting or using Posh Shows is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What success looks like</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hosts receive timely, clear, and helpful support.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Issues are documented accurately, with clear ownership and consistent follow-up.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hosts and internal teams have visibility into open issues and next steps.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Recurring problems lead to actionable recommendations and improvements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Support processes become more efficient as the host community grows.</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT POSHMARK\n\n\nPoshmark is the leading fashion marketplace where style comes alive through discovery, self-expression, and human connection. Powered by a vibrant community of 165 million members, Poshmark brings real people and taste to shopping through a social experience shaped by shared discovery. Buying and selling fashion feels simple, joyful, and personal, while every item tells its own story. Poshmark empowers sellers to grow meaningful businesses, keeps fashion in circulation longer, and gives shoppers access to unique and trusted finds, from everyday pieces to one-of-a-kind vintage and luxury.\n\n \n\nAbout the role\n\nWe’re looking for a Host Operations Specialist to help our hosts run their day-to-day businesses smoothly and support the growth of Posh Live.\n\nIn this role, you’ll own day-to-day host support and coordinate technical issues from initial report through resolution. You’ll work closely with the Account Manager, Product, Engineering, and Customer Support to troubleshoot problems, keep hosts informed, and identify opportunities to improve the host experience.\n\nAs Posh Live grows, you’ll help build the processes and resources that allow us to support more hosts effectively.\n\nWhat you’ll do\n\n - Support hosts with everyday questions and issues. Help hosts navigate product features, show operations, and order-related questions. Resolve issues directly where possible and coordinate with the appropriate teams when additional support is needed.\n\n - Own bug tracking and follow-up. Gather details, reproduce issues where possible, and document clear bug reports, including the impact on hosts’ businesses. Track progress with Product and Engineering and follow through until issues are resolved or a clear next step is established.\n\n - Keep hosts informed. Provide timely updates, explain available workarounds, and close the loop when an issue is resolved.\n\n - Identify recurring problems. Look for patterns across host feedback and support requests, and bring actionable recommendations to the team.\n\n - Improve how we support hosts. Maintain troubleshooting guides, FAQs, and escalation processes to make support faster and more consistent.\n\n - Partner with the Account Manager. Coordinate on host needs and escalations, bringing in account context when needed and ensuring clear ownership of next steps.\n\n - Contribute to business improvements. Work closely with the Posh Live team to identify operational friction that affects hosts’ ability to run shows, fulfill orders, and grow their businesses.\n\nWhat you’ll bring\n\n - Experience in customer support, account operations, marketplace operations, or a similar role.\n\n - Strong problem-solving skills and comfort troubleshooting product and operational issues.\n\n - Strong organization and follow-through, with the ability to manage multiple open issues.\n\n - Clear, empathetic communication with hosts and internal partners.\n\n - Good judgment about urgency, business impact, and when to escalate.\n\n - A proactive mindset and willingness to adapt as the business evolves.\n\n - Familiarity with Poshmark; experience supporting or using Posh Shows is a plus.\n\nWhat success looks like\n\n - Hosts receive timely, clear, and helpful support.\n\n - Issues are documented accurately, with clear ownership and consistent follow-up.\n\n - Hosts and internal teams have visibility into open issues and next steps.\n\n - Recurring problems lead to actionable recommendations and improvements.\n\n - Support processes become more efficient as the host community grows."}],"apiVersion":"1"}